Aegypto mutuati sunt,  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230779F" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Crocodilum</HI>  vocant,
Regem quoque Aegypti nomen draconis hujus gessisse
eruditi ostendunt, quemadmodum ipsa bellua
Aegyptiaci regni typus erat ac symbolum. Porro
quod ex Philone, atque Origene, homil. 2 in Genes.
 <COL N="0779B"></COL> nominis etymon Hieronymus exponit, ab Hebraeo est
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230779G" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skedasthúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">exterminator,</HI>  seu  <HI REND="ITALIC">dissipans.</HI>  Alii  <HI REND="ITALIC">Regem</HI> 
