vel ursus Dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Naphes, refrigerium, vel anima.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nephthali <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0782" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0782A"></COL> In nostro ms.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vel implicuit me, vel dilatavit me.</HI> 
Variae autem sunt apud alios hujusce nominis originationes.
Philo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dianewgmevnon kaiú platusmoún</FOREIGN> : Ammonius
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajntivlhyin,</FOREIGN>  et Hieronymus quoque Quaest.
in Genes. 30,  <HI REND="ITALIC">conversionem comparationemque</HI>  interpretatur.
Rectissime omnium, ut videtur, Joseph.
Antiq. lib. I, cap. 19:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Amhcavnhton,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nullis dolis expugnandum</HI> 
exponit. Nephthalim quippe  <HI REND="ITALIC">strophas</HI>  et
 <HI REND="ITALIC">dolos</HI>  sonant, quemadmodum ex Job cap. V, 13, colligitur:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>boulhún deú poluvplokon</FOREIGN>  (in Hebrai o  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230782D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Nephthalim</HI> )  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxevsthsen.</FOREIGN></NOTE> , conservavit me,
vel dilatavit me, vel certe implicuit
me.</ITEM> <ITEM>Naeth, requiescens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Neman, fidelis, vel motus eorum.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="0782">O.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Orech ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230782A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ) <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0782" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0782B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Orech, longitudo.</HI>  Pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Orech,</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">longitudinem</HI> 
significat, depravate in editis legitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Obeth,</HI>  cujus
nominis nullum exstat in Genesi vestigium. Est autem
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Orech</HI>  civitas regni Nemrod in terra Sennaar,
quae in Vulgata  <HI REND="ITALIC">Arach</HI>  dicitur, ex Hebraei  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230782E" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> . Septuaginta
legunt  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Oreúc</FOREIGN>  Gen. X, 10. Ideoque  <HI REND="ITALIC">Orech</HI> 
hic Scriptum legimus apud Hieronymum, qui in praesenti
opere secutus est Graecam auctoritatem LXX
Translatorum.  <ED>MARTIAN.</ED></NOTE> , longitudo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ochozad, tenens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Olibama, tabernaculum meum
in aliquo, vel tabernaculi altitudo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Odollamites, contestans aliquem,
