consuetudinem veterum Scriptorum secutus eam in
hoc libro mutare noluerit. De nomine vero Israel
ita disserit libro Quaestionum Hebraicarum in Genesim:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Illud autem, quod in libro Nominum interpretatur,</HI> 
 <COL N="0787C"></COL> Israel, vir videns Deum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">omnium pene sermone
detritum, non tam vere, quam violenter mihi interpretatum
videtur. Hic enim</HI>  Israel  <HI REND="ITALIC">per has litteras scribitur,</HI> 
JOD, SIN, RES, ALEPH, LAMED,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod interpretatur,</HI> 
princeps Dei,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sive</HI>  directus Dei,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hoc est,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujquvtatoû Qeouð.</FOREIGN>  Vir  <HI REND="ITALIC">vero</HI>  videns Deum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">his litteris scribitur,</HI> 
ALEPH, JOD, SIN,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut</HI>  vir  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex tribus litteris scribatur, et
 <COL N="0788A"></COL> dicatur</HI>  IS: videns  <HI REND="ITALIC">vero ex tribus,</HI>  RES, ALEPH, HE,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
dicatur</HI>  RA.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Porro</HI>  EL  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex duabus,</HI>  ALEPH, et LAMED,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
interpretatur,</HI>  Deus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sive</HI>  fortis.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quamvis igitur grandis
auctoritatis sint, et eloquentiae ipsorum umbra nos
opprimat, qui</HI>  Israel, virum videntem Deum  <HI REND="ITALIC">transtulerunt:
nos magis Scripturae et Angeli, vel Dei, qui
ipsum</HI>  Israel  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocavit, auctoritatis ducimur, quam cujuslibet
eloquentiae saecularis.</HI>  Hinc videat Lector,
quam imprudenter a quibusdam sciolis Hieronymus
reprehendatur tamquam linguae Hebraicae imperitus,
quod in libris Nominum Hebraicorum et Locorum
ineptas ac violentas etymologias reposuerit: neque
vero in hujusmodi interpretationibus suam profert
sententiam, sed aliorum longe dissimilium ponit
opiniones.  <ED>MARTIAN.</ED></NOTE> , est videre Deum, sive
vir, aut mens videns Deum. Et de
hoc in libris <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0788" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0788A"></COL> Praestat igitur ipsum in hoc libro ad Genes. c.
XXXII. 28, disserentem audire:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Illud autem,</HI>  inquit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quod in libro Nominum interpretatur</HI>  Israel, videns
Deum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">omnium pene sermone detritum, non tam vere,
quam violenter mihi interpretatum videtur. Hic enim</HI> 
 <COL N="0788B"></COL> Israel  <HI REND="ITALIC">per has litteras scribitur,</HI>  IOD, SIN, RES, ALEPH,
LAMED,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod interpretatur</HI>  princeps Dei,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sive</HI>  directus
Dei,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hoc est</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujquvtatoû Qeouð.</FOREIGN>  Vir  <HI REND="ITALIC">vero</HI>  videns Deum,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">his litteris scribitur,</HI>  ALEPH, IOD, SIN,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut</HI>  vir  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex tribus
litteris scribatur, et dicatur</HI>  IS: videns  <HI REND="ITALIC">vero ex tribus,</HI> 
RES, ALEPH, HE,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et dicatur</HI>  RA.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Porro</HI>  El  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex duabus</HI> 
ALEPH et LAMED,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et interpretatur,</HI>  Deus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sive</HI>  fortis.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Quamvis igitur grandis auctoritatis sint, et eloquentiae
ipsorum umbra nos opprimat, qui</HI>  Israel, virum videntem
Deum  <HI REND="ITALIC">transtulerunt: nos magis Scripturae, et Angeli,
vel Dei, qui ipsum</HI>  Israel  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocavit, auctoritate ducimur,
quam cujuslibet eloquentiae saecularis.</HI>  Vide quae
in hunc locum paulo fusius adnotamus.</NOTE>  Hebraicarum Quaestionum
plenius diximus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jethro, superfluus hujus.</ITEM> <ITEM><HI REND=BOLD>21</HI>  Jebusi <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0788" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0788B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Jebusi, calcatus,</HI>  etc. Male legitur in quibusdam
mss.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesubi,</HI>  et in editis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesubaei,</HI>  cum sit ipsum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesubaei,</HI> 
quod in libro Genesis occurrit cum eadem
interpretatione,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jebusaeum, calcatum, sive praesepe
eorum.</HI>   <ED>MARTIAN.</ED> —Ms. noster  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jebusei,</HI>  olim  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesubei.</HI></NOTE> , calceatus, sive
praesepe meum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jamuel, dies ejus Deus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jamin, dextera.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jachin, praeparans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jessaar <NOTE N="m" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0788" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0788B"></COL> Idem videtur esse atque  <HI REND="ITALIC">Issaar</HI>  Numer. 22, 23.
 <COL N="0788C"></COL> quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jassa</HI>  vocat Vulgatus, et Hieronymus quoque
infra ex Numeris. Hebraice  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230788A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> , filius Caath, Exod.
VI, 18. Vide Epist. ad Fabiolam de Mansionibus,
Origenes Homil. in Numeros XIII.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Issaar interpretatur
mandati adimpletio:</HI>  a  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230788B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mandavit,</HI>  et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230788B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cepit,
accepit.</HI></NOTE> , est meridies, sive meridianus,
aut unctio mea, vel  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>metaforikwðû,</FOREIGN> 
oleum.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="0789"></COL> Jochabed, <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0789" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0789A"></COL> Videtur hic de suo exaggerare saepe laudatus
Beda,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jochabed, Domini germen, vel Domini praeparatio,
sive Domini libamen, aut Domini intelligentia:</HI> 
quas ex  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>  Hebraico vocabulo significationes extorquere
violentum est. Vide in Appendice Lexica
Graeca</NOTE>  ubi est gloria, sive
est gravis, aut Domini gloria.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ithamar, ubi amarus, vel ubi
palma, vel est amarus, sive insulae
palma.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jesus ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), salvator.</ITEM> <ITEM>In ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), mensura liquentis materiae.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="0789">L.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Levi, additus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Labeni, filio meo, vel cor ego,
aut candor.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="0789">M.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Mesraim <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0789" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0789A"></COL> Nimis multae sunt, quas ex voce  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mesraim</HI>  etymologias
excudunt Criticorum filii: neque hanc tamen
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hostium</HI>  laudant. Origenian. Lexicon in appendice
pro ea habet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mevlaû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">niger.</HI>  Consentiunt pleraque
alia etiam Latinor. Interpretum, qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">tenebras</HI>  vertunt;
quamquam haec significatio non ex Hebraico
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789E" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> , sed ex Graeco extorta sit.</NOTE>  hostes eorum, vel
Aegyptus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Moses, attrectans, vel palpans,
aut sumptus ex aqua, sive assumptio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Madian, de judicio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Merari, amara, sive amaritudines.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mooli, de infirmitate, sive chorus
meus, aut ab initio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Musi, attrectator, sive palpator
meus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Misael, tactus Dei, sive, quis interrogavit?</ITEM> <ITEM>Magdola ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), quis grandis?
vel turris.</ITEM> <ITEM>Moab, de patre.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mariam, <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0789" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0789A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Mariam, illuminatrix mea,</HI>  etc. Imperfectum est
nomen istud in antea editis libris, ubi legimus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Maria:</HI> 
addendum namque est  <HI REND="ITALIC">m</HI>  in fine, sine quo  <HI REND="ITALIC">Maria</HI> 
non potest habere significationem  <HI REND="ITALIC">maris,</HI>  vel pronominis
 <HI REND="ITALIC">eos,</HI>  ut sciunt Hebraicae linguae periti.  <ED>MARTIAN.</ED></NOTE>  illuminatrix mea, vel
illuminans eos, aut smyrna maris,
vel stella maris.</ITEM> <ITEM>Merra ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), amaritudo.</ITEM> <ITEM>( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ) Marath, amara.</ITEM> <ITEM>Man, <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0789" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0789A"></COL> In nostro ms.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Manhu, quid est hoc?</HI>  Porro notum
 <COL N="0789B"></COL> inde appellari  <HI REND="ITALIC">Manna,</HI>  quod Israelitae eo conspecto
in hanc eruperint vocem  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789F" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> .</NOTE>  quid?</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="0789">N.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Nephthali, latitudo.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="0789"></COL> Nephec, ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789H" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ) pruna, vel carbo,
sive  <HI REND=BOLD>22</HI>  seductio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Neesson, augurans, vel augur
fortis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nadab, spontaneus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nave ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789I" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), semen, germen, vel
pulchritudo.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="0789">O.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Oziel, fortitudo mea Deus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Omer ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Gomor</HI> ), crispans, sive
manipulus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Oliab, protectio mea pater.</ITEM> <ITEM>Oephi ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789J" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), trium modiorum
mensura.</ITEM> <ITEM><HI REND="ITALIC">Nomina quatuor, quae sequuntur,
per extensam legenda sunt litteram.</HI></ITEM> <ITEM>Oreb ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230789K" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), ardor, sive siccitas,
