ms. nostro haec praeponitur admonitio:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Finiunt interpretationes
Hebraicorum Nominum libri Exodi,
inter quas et quae sunt de Levitico</HI>  (perperam vulgati,
ipseque Martianaeus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et quaestiones de Levitico) poteris
invenire, exceptis quatuor, quas subnectere curavimus.</HI> 
Quae quidem verba ab imperitis librariis inducta
idem Martianaeus judicat, ea fortassis de causa,
quod mendose legerit: ego satis vere ac diligenter
annotata sentio, quin ab ipso Hieronymo
scripta tantum non affirmo. Tametsi in subsequenti
nomine, quod mss. atque editi legunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">Badrifath,</HI> 
mendum cubare non inficior.</NOTE>  DE LEVITICO.</HEAD> <LIST COM="0790"><ITEM>Melcho ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Moloch</HI> ), regi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Salumith, retributio, vel pacifica.</ITEM> <ITEM>Fath <NOTE N="l" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0790" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0790B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Fath,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>klivma,</FOREIGN>  etc. Ingens occurrit perturbatio in
antea editis libris, ubi etiam consutum cum textu
 <COL N="0791A"></COL> Hieronymiano legitur sequens additamentum:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Finiunt
interpretationes Hebraicorum Nominum libri
Exodi: inter quas et quaestiones de Levitico potes invenire,
exceptis quatuor, quas subnectere curavimus.</HI> 
Postea sequitur ineptum nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Badrifath,</HI>  interpretatum
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>klivma,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">plaga.</HI>  Sed in vetustioribus mss.
exemplaribus nihil amplius legitur, quam quod a
nobis editum est; et merito, quia caetera ab imperitis
librariis inducta noscuntur, praesertim  <HI REND="ITALIC">Badrifath,</HI> 
cum sola vox  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fath</HI>  mss. codicum sit Hebraeum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230791C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Phath,</HI>  significans  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>klivma,</FOREIGN>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">plagam,</HI>  modo australem,
modo occidentalem. Quod nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Phath</HI>  legitur
saepius in Pentateucho.  <ED>MARTIAN.</ED></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>klivma,</FOREIGN>  id est, plaga: verbi
 <COL N="0791"></COL> gratia cum dicimus, septentrionalis
plaga, vel meridiana.</ITEM></LIST></DIV3> <DIV3 COM="0791" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0791">DE NUMERORUM LIBRO.</HEAD> <LIST COM="0791"><CAPTION COM="0791">A</CAPTION> <ITEM>Ammiod <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0791" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0791A"></COL> Ms. noster praeponit duo isthaec nomina,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aaron
mons fortis. Aminadab populus meus spontaneus:</HI>  quae
quidem et supra recensuimus, sed alterum proprie
ad seriem ex Numeris spectat.</NOTE> , populus meus inclytus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abidan, pater meus judex.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aggelaoni ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeoni</HI> ), annuntiat
iniquitatem meam.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ahiezer, frater meus adjutor.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ammisedai, populus meus sufficiens.</ITEM> <ITEM><HI REND=BOLD>24</HI>  Achran [Ochran,  <HI REND="ITALIC">al.</HI>  Acharan],
turbavit eos.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ahiree, fratris mei amicus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anan, nubes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abia <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0791" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0791A"></COL> Idem cum vetustioribus aliis mss. penes Martian.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Abaia,</HI>  qui rectissime monet legendum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abiu.</HI> 

— <HI REND="ITALIC">Abia, pater meus iste,</HI>  etc. Manuscripti vetustiores,
 <COL N="0791B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Abaja,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abala, pater meus iste.</HI>  Aliquot recentiores
cum editis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abias, pater meus justus,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">juste.</HI> 
At legendum videtur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abiu,</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abiud</HI>  Num. III, 2.
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230791D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abiu</HI>  enim vertitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pater meus iste.</HI>   <ED>MARTIAN.</ED></NOTE> , pater meus iste, vel patris
mei abundantia.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aseroth <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0791" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0791B"></COL> A  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230791E" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> . plurium numero  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230791E" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">atria:</HI>  alia scriptione
ab  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230791E" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">beatitudines</HI>  exprimuntur. Origen.
Hom. 27 in Numer.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aseroth, quod interpretatur atria
perfecta, vel beatitudo.</HI></NOTE> , atrium angustiae, sive
beatitudines.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ammiel, populus meus Dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Amath ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Emath</HI> ), indignatio, vel
uter.</ITEM> <ITEM>Achiman, frater meus quis?</ITEM> <ITEM>Anacim ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Enac</HI> ), monile collo sublimi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aetthi ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230791A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ), obstupefaciens,
sive perterrens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abiram ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Abiron</HI> ), pater meus excelsus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aunan ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Onan</HI> ), non est, vel inutile.</ITEM> <ITEM>Arrad, suscitavit descendens,
