laovn</FOREIGN>  interpretatur lib. de Confusione linguarum.
 <COL N="0792B"></COL> Omitto Origenem cum primis assentientem.</NOTE> , vanus populus, sive
praecipitans eos, vel sine populo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Beor, in pelle:</ITEM> <ITEM>Baal, habens, sive vir.</ITEM> <ITEM>Balfeor, habens os pelliceum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bacher <NOTE N="k" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0792" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0792B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Bacher, in sagmate,</HI>  etc. Idem nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bacher</HI>  sive
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Bochor</HI>  legitur supra cum hac interpretatione in antea
editis libris:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bechor, primogenitus . . . vel ingressus est
angustus;</HI>  quam certe ineptam ultimam etymologiam
