est  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230795E" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> . LXX,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>finwv.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  os meum nepotum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Farnach, vitulus saginatus, aut
discessio mea.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="0795">G.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Gedeoni, <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0795" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0795A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeoni, tentatio humilitatis.</HI>  Editi sic legunt,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeon, tentatio iniquitatis, vel tentatio iniquitatis
meae.</HI>  At  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeon</HI>  sine littera  <HI REND="ITALIC">i</HI>  in fine non potest reddi
eum pronomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">meae.</HI>  Deinde omnes vetustiores
mss. codices habent  <HI REND="ITALIC">humilitatis meae,</HI>  non  <HI REND="ITALIC">iniquitatis
meae;</HI>  nec immerito, cum medium verbum
scribatur per litteram  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ain,</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230795F" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeoni</HI>  Numer.
I, 15.  <ED>MARTIAN.</ED> —Noster ms.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeoni, tentatio
iniquitatis, vel tentatio iniquitatis meae.</HI>  Concinunt
veteres editi, qui tamen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeon</HI>  habent pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gedeoni.</HI></NOTE>  tentatio iniquitatis,
