parturiens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Arth ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Haret</HI> ), mora.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abiathar, pater superfluus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Achela ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Hachila</HI> ), suspiciens
eam.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abigal, pater exsultationis, sive
 <NOTE N="g" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0812" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0812A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Abigal, pater roris.</HI>  Editi libri,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pater erroris:</HI>  sed
verius legitur in manuscriptis, quia auctor hujus
libri respexit ad nomen  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230812C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Abital,</HI>  quod reddi
potest,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pater roris,</HI>  non  <HI REND="ITALIC">pater erroris.</HI>   <ED>MARTIAN.</ED> 

—Ms. noster, cum pridem editis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pater erroris.</HI> 
 <COL N="0813A"></COL> Conjicit Martian. ad nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abital,</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230813C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> , quod
redditur  <HI REND="ITALIC">pater roris,</HI>  hujus libri auctorem respexisse.
