regis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anamelech, respondenti regi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abisa <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Abisa, voluntas mea in ea.</HI>  Corruptum est nomen
 <COL N="0823B"></COL> istud  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abisa,</HI>  ut ex significatione seu interpretatione
liquido apparet; non enim  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abisa</HI>  legendum est, sed
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Aphsiba,</HI>  quod satis innuunt Graeca exemplaria in
quibus scribitur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ayibaú</FOREIGN>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ofeibaú.</FOREIGN>  Hebraice est
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230823C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hhaphsiba;</HI>  idque Latine dicitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">voluntas mea
in ea.</HI>  Eadem vox infra occurrit sub littera E, ubi
etiam editi legebant  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ebsiba</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ephsiba,</HI>  ob pronuntiationem,
ni fallor, veterum librariorum, qui audientes
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ephsiba,</HI>  putabant se audire  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ebsiba</HI>  cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">b,</HI> 
propter affinitatem sonorum in illis consonantibus.
Caeterum soloecismus est in interpretatione jam
dictae vocis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ephsiba,</HI>  tam in editis libris quam in
manuscriptis: legunt enim prononem masculinum
 <COL N="0824A"></COL> tertiae personae singularis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">voluntas mea in eo:</HI>  cum
ex affixo Hebraeo feminino  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230824D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>  in fine, verbum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230824D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Hapsi-ba</HI>  necessario interpretari debeamus  <HI REND="ITALIC">voluntas
mea in ea.</HI>   <ED>MARTIAN.</ED> 

