deserta.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sobnas, sedens, vel revertens.</ITEM> <ITEM><HI REND="ITALIC">Saesdema</HI> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0827" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0827A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Saesdema, pestilens aer.</HI>  Lege  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sedema,</HI>  quod est
singulare nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sademoth</HI>  post pauca hic positi.
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Sedema</HI>  autem idem significat ac  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Sedepha,</HI> 
et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Sedephon,</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Siddaphon;</HI>  quod Hieronymus
lib. III Reg. VIII, 37, interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">corruptum
aerem,</HI>  id est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnemofqorivan.</FOREIGN>  Ubi vero sit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Saesdema</HI> 
lib. IV Regum nequeo divinare:  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Sadepha</HI>  legitur
cap. XIX, 26.  <ED>MARTIAN.</ED> 

—Quod Graeci  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnemofqorivan,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">uredinem,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">corruptionem
aeris</HI>  vocant. Hebraice  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sciddaphon</HI> 
appellatur.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Saesdema,</HI>  quod Hieronymus legit, ipsum
videtur  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">scedema,</HI>  IV Regum XIX, 26.
quod ibi in Hebraicis exemplaribus  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">scedepha</HI> 
scribitur  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>  scilicet in  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0230827D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>  quae ejusdem organi
 <COL N="0827B"></COL> est littera, commutato. Re autem ipsa  <HI REND="ITALIC">scedepha</HI>  legendum
hic quoque loci est juxta Hebraeum textum,
ut quoquo modo  <HI REND="ITALIC">pestilentis aeris</HI>  expositio congruat;
sciendumque ipsum  <HI REND="ITALIC">scedepha</HI>  loco ex IV Regum laudato
ita scriptum esse pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">scedema,</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">agrum</HI>  sonat.
Fuerit olim in hoc ipso Nominum libro ad
hunc modum:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sedepha, pestilens aer,</HI>  etc. Studiosus
 <COL N="0828A"></COL> nonnemo ad libri oram annotarit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sedema,</HI>  ut pro
hac voce illam in Hebraico scribi indicaret: calligraphus
vero hanc illi debere substitui ratus, altera
expuncta, alteram corruperit.</NOTE> , pestilens aer: quam
Graeci significantius  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnemofqorivan</FOREIGN> 
vocant.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sarasar princeps tribulationis</ITEM> <ITEM>Saphan ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Saphan</HI> ), labium ejus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sademoth  <CITN>(Apud LXX, XXIII, 5)</CITN> ,
arva, vel regiones.</ITEM> <ITEM>Saraia, vinctus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Saphania, abscondit Dominus,
