oblationem</HI>  exprimi volunt, teste etiam Hieronymo,
qui hujusmodi etymologiam penitus non approbat,
dicens  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jessai</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">Essai</HI>  melius significare  <HI REND="ITALIC">incensum,</HI> 
quam  <HI REND="ITALIC">insulae libamen.</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231158A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">i</HI>  porro insulam significat,
et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231158A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">isse, incensum,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">sacrificium,</HI>  unde nomen
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231158A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Jessai</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Essai</HI>  deductum statuunt.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>nhvsou kavrpwma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwshúf,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1158" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1158B"></COL> Facile rescribendum videatur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prosqhvswn,</FOREIGN>  quod et
Clerico placet.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prosthvqwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ierousalhúm, oårasiû eijrhvnhû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iskariwúq</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1158" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1158A"></COL> Memoria mortis potest Iscarioth interpretari,
modo figuratum intelligatur ex  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231158B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">zecher,</HI>  id est,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">memoria,</HI>  et ex  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231158B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Karath,</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">exterminium</HI>  vel
 <HI REND="ITALIC">abscisionem</HI>  sonat. Confer quae supra de hoc nomine
