aujtwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Korbaðn, prosforaú, hÞ dwðron</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1158" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1158B"></COL> Colbertin. addit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtoú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsum.</HI></NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kananaiðoû, kekthmevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Labbaiðoû, kardiva,</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1159"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mariaúm,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1159" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1159B"></COL> Sic emendat Vatic. Legerat vero Martian. ex
Regio satis corrupte  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wjtivzousa,</FOREIGN>  verteratque in Latino
 <HI REND="ITALIC">audiens,</HI>  quam expositionem tamen in subnexa annotatione
respuit his verbis: Violenter admodum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mariam</HI> 
interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">audiens;</HI>  etymologiamque hujuscemodi
amputatam ab Hieronymo minime diffitebar,
sed inspecto Origenis Lexico inveni scriptum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fwtivzousa,</FOREIGN> 
id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">illuminatrix.</HI>  Legamus igitur non  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wjtivzousa,</FOREIGN> 
sed  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fwtivzousa.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fwtivzousa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1159" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1159B"></COL> Ms. Colbertin.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Matqaivoû, dwmatsiqevntoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Matthaeus,
donati.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Matqaiðon,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1159" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1159A"></COL> Quid sit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dwmatisqevnta</FOREIGN>  non facile dixerim. Nonnulli
mecum putant legendum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>domatisqevnta,</FOREIGN>  a  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dovma</FOREIGN> :
et hoc sensu interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">donatum.</HI>  Quae conjectura
non est improbabilis; si tamen conjectura est, et
non genuinae potius lectionis restiturio.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dwmatisqevnta.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Magdalhnhú, ejk puvrgou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nazareút, ajkrevmonoû aujtouð, hÞ kaqarovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nazoraiðoû, kaqarovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nazhraiðoû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1159" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1159B"></COL> Perperam ex Regio ms. Martianaeus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxisqismevnoû</FOREIGN> 
legit, et interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">obstupefactus,</HI>  quod nullo
 <COL N="1159C"></COL> pacto nomini, sive radici  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nazar</HI>  possit aptari. Restituimus
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxhnqismevnoû</FOREIGN>  ex Vaticano exemplari, quod in
Latino sonat  <HI REND="ITALIC">floribus variegatus,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">distinctus:</HI>  notum
quippe ex subsequenti etiam titulo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nazar</HI>  Hebraice
 <HI REND="ITALIC">florem</HI>  significare.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxhnqismevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1159" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1159A"></COL> Eadem verba posita reperies in Fragmento V,
cum variantibus lectionibus. Primo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Navzar,</FOREIGN>  non  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aænqh</FOREIGN> 
in plurali, sed  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aænqoû,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">flos</HI>  interpretatur. Secundo
nulla ibi statuitur differentia inter verbum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nazoraiðoû</FOREIGN> 
et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nazhraiðoû</FOREIGN> ; ut revera nulla est, sive per  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>o,</FOREIGN> 
sive er  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>h</FOREIGN>  scribatur. Denique quae citata sunt in voce
sequenti  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nefqaliúm,</FOREIGN>  hoc modo leguntur in codice ms.
fol. 72:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nefqaleivm ajntivlhyiû, kaiú Nefqaliúm sunanevsteyevn
me,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nephthaleim, opitulatio, et Nephthalim,
convertit me.</HI>  Abundat ergo vox  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajorajtou</FOREIGN>  praesentis
loci juxta fidem recitatae etymologiae, licet in voce
Nephtalim fingi possit nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eloim,</HI>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dei,</HI>  vel
 <HI REND="ITALIC">invisibilis,</HI>  esse comprehensum.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Navzar,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160B"></COL> Minori numero  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aænqoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">flos,</HI>  fecimus ex Vaticano.
Antea erat minus recte  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aænqh,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">flores.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aænqoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nefqaliúm, sunanevstreyevn me,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160B"></COL> Quod hinc subsequitur Graeculi annotatoris glossema,
