touðto.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pontivou, klivnantoû boulhvn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pilavtou, stovma</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1159" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1159A"></COL> Absentia unius litterulae multum diuque me tutudit
in hac voce  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sfurokovpou,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">tundentis,</HI>  et
 <COL N="1159B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">malleatoris:</HI>  corrupte enim scribitur in codice Regio
 <COL N="1160A"></COL> sine  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>s</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Sigma</HI>  initiali  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>furokovpou,</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sfurokovpou.</FOREIGN> 
Est autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">sphurocopos, malleator</HI>  juxta quod scriptum
legimus Gen. IV. 22:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaiú høn sfurokovpoû calkeuúû
calkouð kaiú sidhvrou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Et fuit malleator, faber aeris et
ferri.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sfurokovpou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pevtroû, ejpiluvwn,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160B"></COL> In Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hæ dialuvwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vel dissolvens.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ dialuvsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ramað</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="g" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160B"></COL> Postea observavit Martianaeus legi in Colbertin.
cod.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ramaú uJywvqh, hÞ ajrchú uJyhlhv</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Rama exaltata, vel
imperium sublime.</HI>  Videturque illi ex Regii ms. lectione,
quae eadem ac Vaticani est, subintelligi usitatissimam
in Sacra Scriptura phrasim,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Exaltetur manus
tua,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">In manu excelsa,</HI>  etc. Colbertinum vero
pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Rama</HI>  interpretari nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Rama,</HI>  cujus  <HI REND="ITALIC">principatus</HI> 
 <COL N="1160C"></COL> fuit omnium  <HI REND="ITALIC">excelsissimus.</HI></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJywvqh hJ ceivr.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rachúl, provbaton.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Raaúb, ejplatuvnqh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rouúq, speuvdousa, hÞ oJrwðsa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rakaú, kenev,</FOREIGN>  al.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kenovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rabbeiú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160C"></COL> Martian.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Rambeiv,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Rambi,</HI>  manifesto ac saepe obvio
codicis Regii,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>m</FOREIGN>  ponentis pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>b,</FOREIGN>  vitio.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>didavskalev mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sidwún</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160C"></COL> Colbertin  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Shdwú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Scdo.</HI></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qhvreuma</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160A"></COL> Non minorem quam superior attulit molestiam
vox  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnwfeleúû</FOREIGN>  quae in ms. codice legitur cum Lambda,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajlwfelevû</FOREIGN> : quod undecumque versum nihil significare
potest.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sidon</HI>  autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">captura.</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">venatio inutilis</HI>  vertitur;
quia  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231160A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">seda,</HI>  venationem sonat, et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231160A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">on</HI>  sive
 <HI REND="ITALIC">aun,</HI>  inutilem.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnwfelevû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Toú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160A"></COL> Graeca interdum Hebraeis admiscent auctores
Graeci vel exscriptores, in novo praecipue Testamento,
cujus nomina supplevit Origenes, recensens Latina
Graecaque vocabula juxta proprietatem linguae Hebraicae.
Salis porro et carnis fit memio in contextu
Graeco Matth. V. 13, et XVI, 17, etc.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aålaû, taú aåla.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Toú krevaû, toú kreva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Taliqaú koumiú, taú koravsion aJnavsthqi.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cananaiðoi, metavboloi.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1159"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>EN TW KATA MARKON EUAGGELIW.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Arimaqaiðoû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Armathaeus</HI>  melius interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">altitudo ejus</HI> 
quam  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsorum:</HI>  unde pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtouð</FOREIGN>  Graece scriptum videtur
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðn.</FOREIGN></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåyouû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1160" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1160C"></COL> Erat ex Regio  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Arimatqaiðoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Arimatthaeus:</HI>  minus
 <COL N="1161B"></COL> recte. Alteram vero addit Colbertin. etymologiam
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrwðn ejkeiðno, eJtoimovthû,</FOREIGN>  quam Martian. interpretatur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">arans illud, dispositio:</HI>  sed quid sibi velit. atque
unde illam hauserint Graeci ignorare se profitetur.
Nihil tamen insit difficultatis, si  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrwðn</FOREIGN>  ab  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aiærw</FOREIGN>  deduci
intelligas, ac vertas  <HI REND="ITALIC">subvehens,</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">extollens illud.</HI> 
Hieronymus quoque.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Arimatthaeus,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">altitudo
ejus, vel exaltatus est ipse.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1161"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abbað, pathúr, hÞ patrovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bartimaiðoû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1161" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1161A"></COL> Corrupte  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bartimaeus</HI>  scriptum legitur apud Graecos
pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Barsemia,</HI>  ut docuit nos sanctus Hieronymus
supra in Nominibus de Joanne. Verum ex isto Origeniani
Lexici fragmento manifestissime comprobatur,
nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bartimaeus,</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Barsemia</HI>  legendum in Marco,
non in Joanne. Consule superiores annotationes nostras
in hocce vocabulo.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uiJoúû tuflovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Boanhrgeúû, uiJoúû bronthðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beelzebouúl, katapivnwn muivaû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Israhúl</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1161" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1161A"></COL> Habe, hoc loco etymologiam nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Israel,</HI> 
quam S. Hieronymus erudite confutat libro Quaestionum
Hebraicarum in Genesim, et alibi saepe.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnhúr blevpwn qeouð, hÞ nouðû
oJrwðn qeovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1161" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1161B"></COL> Colbertinus concinniori ordine nomen  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Effaqav</FOREIGN>  nomini
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Israhúl</FOREIGN>  praeponit.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Effaqaú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1161" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1161A"></COL> Licet ordo servetur elementorum in hoc Fragmento
libri Nominum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ephphetha</HI>  nihilominus positum
legimus post litteram I, quia prima syllaba hujus
vocis servilis est apud Syros et apud Hebratos, characteristica
conjugationis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ethpael.</HI>  Perinde est igitur
ac si verbum incipiat abs radicali  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231161A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">pha.</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">phe.</HI> 
Hinc in contextu jam edito sancti Hieronymi, ultimum
verbum in Marco est ipsum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Phata</HI>  absque ulla
 <COL N="1162A"></COL> servili particula: quod minime veteres editores assecuti,
vocem ac ordinem ejus perturbarunt, ut antea
monuimus.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dianoivcqhti.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1161"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>EN TW KATA LOUKAN EUAGGELIW.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aujgouvstou, eJortavzontoû, hÞ eJorthún
prostiqemevnou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abiaú, pathvr mou kuvrioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aarwún, oæroû dunavmewû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Amhún, pepistwmevnoû gevnoito.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Annaú, cavriû aujtouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aggeú, eJorthv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Adaiú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1161" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1161B"></COL> Idem Colbertin., cum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>d</FOREIGN>  gemino,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Addaiv.</FOREIGN></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ iJkanovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Enwúc, ejgkainismovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Enwúû, aænqrwpoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Emmaouúû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1161" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1161B"></COL> Ex Vatic. et Colbertin. legimus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Emmaouvû,</FOREIGN>  ipso
