 <HI REND="ITALIC">fetus pulchritudinis.</HI>  Sed et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nhneuiè</FOREIGN>  habet pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nineuhð.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gonhðû wJraiovthû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rama, uJyhlhðé.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sarefqaú, purwdhðû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1163" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1163B"></COL> In Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>purwthv.</FOREIGN></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ qlivyiû aærtou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>SiJmwn, ajkouvwn luvphn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sovdoma, bovskhma,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1163" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1163A"></COL> Similiter et Sodoma dicitur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>puvrwsiû,</FOREIGN>  quia igne
coelesti ac ultricibus flammis absumpta est;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>puvrwsiû</FOREIGN> 
est etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">incendium.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ povrwsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sataðn, ajntikeivmenoû, hÞ ajpostavthû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabaú, aijcmalwsiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1163" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1163A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Tiberius</HI>  melius vertitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">visio ejus,</HI>  quam  <HI REND="ITALIC">visionis
