interpretati sunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">rubeum,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">roboreum.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ druviçnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Roubiúm,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1167" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1167A"></COL> Falsus est hic loci scriptor Graecus in compendio
litterarum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pra</FOREIGN> ; non enim  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>r,</FOREIGN>  sed  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>n</FOREIGN>  scribere debuit
in medio,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pna,</FOREIGN>  ut sit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pneuðma</FOREIGN>  juxta veram Graecorum
lectionem, qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ruben</HI>  interpretantur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Spiritum
Dei,</HI>  id est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pneuðma qeouð.</FOREIGN>  Vide infra in Lexico Origeniano.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pra qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sumewðn, uJpakouvwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Leuiú, uJpeúr ejmouð mehsqeuvsei.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iouvdaû, ejxomolovghsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Isavcar, misqovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1168" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1168A"></COL> Male et violenter in hoc libro Nominum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Zabulon,
fluxus noctis,</HI>  interpretatum declarat Hieronymus,
quem consuli velim libro Quaest. Hebraicarum
in Genesim, ubi omnium Patriarcharum etymologias
nominum voluit pariter dicere.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Zabouloún, dwðron.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Daún, krivsiû</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nefqaleiúm, ajntivlhyiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gaúd, ejpivteugma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ashúr, makarismovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwshúf, prosqhvkh,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1168" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1168A"></COL> Hoc loco male scriptum est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oæneida,</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ojneideiva</FOREIGN> 
sive  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ojneidiva.</FOREIGN>  Quod autem in tam contrarias significationes
apud Graecos nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joseph</HI>  commutetur,
non aliunde evenit quam ex diverso themate,
seu diversa Hebraea radice,  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231168A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">jasaph</HI>  namque
idem apud Hebraeos quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">addidit;</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231168A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">suph</HI>  autem
 <HI REND="ITALIC">terminavit</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">consumpsit</HI>  significat: unde apud Arabas
remanet  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231168B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sajaph,</HI>  quod sonath  <HI REND="ITALIC">obtruncavit
caput.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÝ oæneidoû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1168" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1168A"></COL> Legerat Martian.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hæ oæneida</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oæneidoû.</FOREIGN></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ
ajfaivresiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beniamiún,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1168" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1168A"></COL> Quia Benjamin vocatus est a matre  <HI REND="ITALIC">Benoni,</HI>  id
est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">filius doloris,</HI>  Graeci linguae Hebraicae imperiti
putarunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">Benjamin</HI>  sonare  <HI REND="ITALIC">filium doloris.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tevknon ojduvnhû, hÞ uiJoúû dexiaðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Melcisedeúk, ajpovstoloû divkaioû, hÞ</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1168" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1168A"></COL> Idem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>basilikoúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">regius,</HI>  excudit pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>basileuúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">rex.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>basileuúû divkaioû, hÞ eijrhneuvwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1167"><COL N="1169"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI ROUBIM.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Roubiúm,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1169A"></COL> Continua hic est nominum depravatio, et interpretationum
perturbatio. Rubenis enim etymologia
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qaumastoúû,</FOREIGN>  hoc est  <HI REND="ITALIC">mirabilis,</HI>  consequentis est
nominis  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>feloúc,</FOREIGN>  quod in Hebraeo scriptum est  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231169A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Phallu,</HI>  mitabilemque significat. Praeterea  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tovxon aijwvnion</FOREIGN> 
pertinet ad nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hesron</HI>  omissum ab exscriptore,
dum recenset filios Ruben. Caetera praetereo,
quia ex comparatione textus Hieronymiani perspicua
sunt lectori. Consulendum tamen nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ezrom</HI> 
infra in praesenti Fragmento.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qaumastovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Feloúc, tovxon aijwvnion.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1169B"></COL> Denuo idem pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cavrmin</FOREIGN>  legerat  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Carmeún</FOREIGN> ; quae
emendat Vaticanus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cavrmin, aæmpelon mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1169"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI SUMEWN.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iemouhúl, dexiaú ijscurouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iemiún, dexiav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1169A"></COL> Nullus inter filios Simeon recensetur in Genesi,
qui vocetur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Oli,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bana:</HI>  nec hujusmodi vocabula
leguntur apud Hieronymum sub illa forma. Proclive
est ut credamus. ex nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Oolibama</HI>  veterum exscriptorum
errore derivata fuisse vocabula  <HI REND="ITALIC">Oli et Bana:</HI> 
at  <HI REND="ITALIC">Oolibama</HI>  non est nomen viri, sed mulieris, uxoris
Esau.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Wliú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1169B"></COL> Vatic. quae hinc subsequuntur nomina ita per
seriem effert:

 <LIST COM="1169"><ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Weúl, skhvnwma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iachúl, eåtoimoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Banaú, leukovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM></LIST></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skhvnwma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Banaú, leukovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iachúl, eåtoimoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1169"><NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1169B"></COL> Hanc epigraphen:

 <CAPTION COM="1169"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIO1I LEUEI,</FOREIGN></CAPTION> 

quae Graeculi amanuensis incuria in Regio ms. desiderabatur,
et Martianaeus non animadvertit, ex
 <COL N="1170B"></COL> Vatic. ms. suffecimus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI LEUEI.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Leueiú,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1169A"></COL> Pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtoúû</FOREIGN>  legendum videtur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uiJoiú,</FOREIGN>  juxta seriem
contextus sacri, Gen., XLVI. 11; saltem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðé,</FOREIGN>  id est  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsi,</HI> 
 <COL N="1169B"></COL> non  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipse</HI>  legendum monet Hebraicum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231169B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> , in quo est
particula  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231169B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">lo,</HI>  quae Graece redditur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðé.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ghrsaún, pavroikoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaaúq, ejkklhsiasthvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Merariú, pikrainovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1169"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI IOUDA.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>5Hr, drumoúû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1170B"></COL> Male interpretatur Martian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi belluae,</HI>  ait Clericus,
quasi  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qhriwvdouû</FOREIGN>  idem esset ac  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qhriva.</FOREIGN>  Sed lege
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tovpou qhriwvdouû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">loci feris relicti,</HI>  constabuntque; et
sensus et constructio.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåpou qhriwvdouû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aujnaðn, phghv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Shlwúm, ajnomiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Fareúû, fraguovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Zazaú, ejpifanhvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1169"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI ISACAR.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qwdaú, skwvlhx.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Fouaú, wßdev eijmi.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwúb, ajgaphtovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Swlomwún, throuvmenon.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1169"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI ZABOULWN.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Zaboulwún,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1169B"></COL> Forte legi debet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujodwðn,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">prosperum iter
 <COL N="1170A"></COL> praebens,</HI>  sive ab  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujodevw,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">expeditum iter habens.</HI>  Quae
etymologia satis convenit nomini Zabulon, quod
alibi  <HI REND="ITALIC">fluens</HI>  interpretatur. Certe  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujwvdwm</FOREIGN>  corruptum
verbum est, quocumque sensu sumatur.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujwvdwm</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1170B"></COL> Rescribi malim  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujodmoúû,</FOREIGN>  quod est  <HI REND="ITALIC">odorus,</HI>  sive
 <HI REND="ITALIC">odoratus.</HI>  In Vatic. autem exemplari  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujovdwmoû</FOREIGN>  scriptum
videtur, postremo litterarum ductu ob vetustatem
oculos fugiente, quae causa exstiterit Regii
codicis exscriptori, ut solum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eujwvdwm</FOREIGN>  repraesentaret.</NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Seeúr, pepaideumevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1170A"></COL> <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231170A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Elon</HI>  Graeci confuse accipiunt pro  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231170A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">elom,</HI> 
quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">saeculum</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">sempiternum</HI>  significat.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elwúm, aijwvnioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1170A"></COL> Non poterat clarius aut efficacius probari nominum
propriorum corruptela, de qua Origenes et Hieronymus
tam saepe conqueruntur, quam ista praesenti
vocabulorum serie vitiosa: major enim est
caeteris omnibus depravationibus nominum, quae in
editis Graecis exemploribus visuntur. Ecquis crederet
nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joalel.</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jahelel</HI>  ad tantam corruptelam
prolapsum temeritate, vel oscitantia veterum
exscriptorum, ut pro eo legeretur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Geel;</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sephion,
Sedon;</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Arodi, Varilei,</HI>  et sic de reliquis, quorum
foeditatem ex comparatione Hieronymianae tabulae
lector facile deprehendet? Sed praeter illam
 <COL N="1170B"></COL> depravationis speciem, aliae sunt in codice manuscripto,
ut cum legimus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uiJoiú Daún,</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uiJoiú Gaúd</FOREIGN> ; et
vicissim,  <HI REND="ITALIC">filii Gaad,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">filii Dan. Usim</HI>  namque solus
 <COL N="1171A"></COL> filius est Dan; Sephion autem cum reliquis filius
fuit Patriarchae Gad. Hoc nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gad</HI>  ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">Usim</HI> 
scriptum legitur in columna Hieronymiana propter
solam comparationem diversae etymologiae: nec
sum tam hebetis cordis, ut recenseam  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gad</HI>  inter filios
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Dan.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gehúl</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1170B"></COL> Hic in Vatic. ms. sub seric filiorum Dan recensetur.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæleoû kurivou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1169"><COL N="1171"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI DAN.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sedoún ejpivskopoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aggeiú, eJortasmovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Swmivein, deuterwthvû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Iesbaú, duvnamivû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1171" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1171B"></COL> In Vatic. scribitur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mhvre,</FOREIGN>  et paulo post uno verbo
et veluri singulare alterum nomen  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qouarileið</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qwuð
1Arileið.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mevre, mavrtuû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Oujarileið katavbasivû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qouð 1Arileið, hJ fuvsiû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1171"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI NEFQALEIM.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nefqaleiúm, proseuchv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Asahúl, ijscuúû patroúû ijscurouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gwnivei, ajp1 ejmouð aijwvnioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iessaaúr, ijscurovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qusilhúm, tevleioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1171"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI GAAD.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1171" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1171A"></COL> Ne actum saepius agamus, et eadem semper replicemus,
meminerit Lector superiorum annotationum
nostrarum, quibus ostensum est, verba Hebraica,
nequaquam secundum proprietatem linguae, aut
fidem elementorum, ubique a Graecis esse interpretata;
ut etiam ex nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gad</HI>  jam perspicue liquet,
quod interpretantur  <HI REND="ITALIC">venientem.</HI>  Sed audiendus hac
de re Hieronymus:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ubi nos,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">posuimus, in
fortuna, et Graece dicitur</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn tuvché,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quae potest eventus
dici, in Hebraeo habet</HI>  BAGAD ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231171A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod Aquila interpretatur,
venit accinctio. Nos autem dicere possumus,
in procinctu.</HI>  BA  <HI REND="ITALIC">enim potest praepositionem sonare</HI> 
in,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  venit.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ab eventu ergo sive procinctu, qui</HI> 
GAD  <HI REND="ITALIC">dicitur. Zelpha filius Gad vocatus est. Gad</HI>  itaque
 <COL N="1171B"></COL> interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">accinctio,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">ba, venit.</HI>  Quod imperitiam
Graecorum effugit, qui legentes forte apud Aquilam,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">venit accinctio,</HI>  suspicati sunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gad</HI>  Hebraice idem
 <COL N="1172A"></COL> esse quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">venire,</HI>  cujus opinionis inscitiam castigat
Hieronymus libro Quaest. Heb. in Genesim a nobis
modo citato. Similes mox occurrunt in aliis nominibus
etymologiae Graecorum, quas sigillatim Notis illustrare
non suscepi, ne cum in has Grammaticorum
tricas sumptus insumo, a potioribus ipsae ac
magis necessartis animum meum avocent, remoramque
pariant diligentiae gravissimis rebus impertiendae.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gaúd, ejrcovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Queiúm, eijkasmovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1171"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI ASHR.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ashúr, makavrioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Emmaú, ajriqmouvmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1172" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1172A"></COL> In Graeca hujus nominis etymologia legendum
videtur non  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxiouvmenoû,</FOREIGN>  sed  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxiwvmenoû</FOREIGN>  ab  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxiwðmai,</FOREIGN>  quod
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sonare</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">sancire</HI>  significat. Quo sensu  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jasua,</HI>  sive
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesua,</HI>  non abs re dicitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">sanans,</HI>  utpote  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui pertransiit
benefaciendo,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ijwvmenoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et sanando omnes oppressos
a diabolo.</HI>  Act. X, 38. In Latina autem interpretatione.
Hieronymi illud pariter observandum, secundam
etymologiam nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesua, est desiderium
meum,</HI>  ad vocabulum sequens magis pertinere; quia
in  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231172A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Jessui,</HI>  pronomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">meum</HI>  invenitur, quod in
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231172A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesua</HI>  non legimus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iavsoua,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1171" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1171B"></COL> Vatic. plurium numero,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxiouvmenoi.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxiouvmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iasouvh, ajxivwmav mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Oujkriva, dunatovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Oujsehúl, perisseuomevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1171"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI IOSHF.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwshúf, provsqesiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Efrai0m, platuvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Manasshðû, pepramevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Asseneúq, misouvmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1172" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1172B"></COL> Idem Vatic.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pettefrhð.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Petefrhð, oJratovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1171"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI BENIAMIN.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beniamiún, uiJoúû dexiovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salaiú, katapeinovmenoû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1172" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1172B"></COL> Legendum videtur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katapeinwvmenoû,</FOREIGN>  a radice  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peinavw</FOREIGN> :
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peivnw</FOREIGN>  enim a lexicis abest.  <ED>ED.</ED></NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabacaúr, prwtovtokoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sebhúr, puðr ejrcovmenon.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Peraú, paroikeiðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nabauð, yavllwn hJdevwû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1172" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1172B"></COL> Corruptelas horum nominum in Graeco redarguere
possumus ab ipsa interpretatione.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Leis,</HI>  exempli
gratia, interpretatum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajdelfovû mou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">frater meus,</HI> 
 <COL N="1173A"></COL> manifestissime ducet pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Leis</HI>  legendum ac scribendum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Echi,</HI>  quod Hebraice dicitur  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231173A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Echi,</HI>  vel
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ahhi,</HI>  significatque  <HI REND="ITALIC">fratrem meum.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Leiúû, ajdelfovû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1173"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ouæaroû, ajochgovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1173" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1173A"></COL> Ex Graeco et Hebraeo facta videtur etymologia
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Momphin</HI>  apud Graecos.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Morfhú</FOREIGN>  enim Graecis est  <HI REND="ITALIC">species</HI> 
oris, et affixum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231173B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">i,</HI>  Hebraeis est pronomen
primae personae sing. masc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">meus:</HI>  hinc  <HI REND="ITALIC">Momphi,</HI> 
vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">Morphi</HI>  potest dici apud Graecos linguae Hebraicae
incuriosos,  <HI REND="ITALIC">similitudo mea.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Momfiún, oJmoiovthû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qouaraú, katavbasivû mou</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1173" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1173A"></COL> Addit Vatic. hic vocem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxovdou</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Exodi:</HI>  tum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pivqwn,</FOREIGN> 
pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pivqwm</FOREIGN>  legit.</NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pivqwm, stovma aijwvnion.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ramesshú, aJrpaghv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Semfovra, ejpivskeyiû wJraiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Fouaú, profhvthû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Leueiúd, uJpourgovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mwuçshúû, uådatoû ajnaivresiû, hÞ nouúû
eujsebhúû, hÞ eæreuna kurivou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ragouhúl,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1173" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1173A"></COL> Pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fivloû</FOREIGN>  legerat Martian.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iælloû,</FOREIGN>  quae vox Ionica
dialecto  <HI REND="ITALIC">oculum</HI>  sonat. Atque ita quidem vertit,
rationemque ejus etymi hanc reddit: Propter priorem
syllabam  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ra, oculi,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">visus</HI>  significantiam extorquent
 <COL N="1173B"></COL> Graeci e nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Raguel;</HI>  non intelligentes
scriptum esse vocabulum cum littera  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231173D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Ain,</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231173D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <COL N="1174A"></COL> non  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> .

Verum puto luce meridiana clarius est, emendandum,
uti fecimus, ex Vatican.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fivloû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">amicus:</HI>  juxta
Hebraicam analogiam, et Hieronymi interpretationem,
qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">pastionem</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">amicum</HI>  vertit, et tam saepe
alibi docuit, iisdem litteris  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> , et  <HI REND="ITALIC">pastorem</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">amicum</HI> 
 <COL N="1174B"></COL> denotari.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fivloû ijscurovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwqwúr, perisseiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Zwfhúq, zwhú plateiða.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1173"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI FARES.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1173" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1173A"></COL> Confer nomen istud cum nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pheloch</HI>  supra
posito, ut testis ipse accedas,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tovxon aijwvnion</FOREIGN>  esse etymologium
vocabuli  <HI REND="ITALIC">Esrom,</HI>  non nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pheloch.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Esrwúm. tovxon aijwvnion.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Amouúl, eæleoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1173"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI EFRAIM.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Souqalaú, ajxivwma ajpostolikovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1174" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1174B"></COL> In Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>becavr.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Becoúr, prwtovtokoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1173"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI MANASSH.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Galaaúd, marturiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1173"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>UIOI BRIA.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1173" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1173A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Eber</HI>  scriptum cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ain</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231173C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>  ab initio significat
 <COL N="1174A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">transitorem;</HI>  si autem habeat  <HI REND="ITALIC">Heth</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> , interpretatur
 <HI REND="ITALIC">amicus,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">socius</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">conjunctus.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ebeúr, fivloû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1174" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1174A"></COL> Nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mathusalae</HI>  etymologiam vocabulo  <HI REND="ITALIC">Melchiel</HI> 
affigere hoc loco Graeci videntur, licet  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Melchiel</HI>  possit aliquo modo interpretari  <HI REND="ITALIC">missus,</HI>  si
figuratam sive formatam dicamus vocem a verbo
Chaldaico  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">malach,</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">nuntium</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">missum</HI>  sonat
apud Orientales. Hinc Targumistae verbum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">malach,</HI>  Prov. XIII, 17, reddunt per  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">scelihha,</HI> 
derivatum a verbo  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231174B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">salahh,</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">mittere</HI>  significat.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Melcihúl, ajpestalmevnoû ajpoú ijscurouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM></LIST></DIV2> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="1173"><HEAD COM="1173"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hieronymus.
Liber nominum Hebraicorum.</HI></HEAD> <COL N="1166"></COL> <LIST COM="1166"><ITEM>Adam, homo, sive terrenus; aut
indigena, vel terra rubra.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abba, pater. Syrum est.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abel, luctus, sive vanitas; vel vapor,
aut miserabilis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Cain, possessio, vel lamentatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Seth, positio, vel positus; aut poculum,
sive gramen; aut semen,
sive resurrectio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Enos, homo; sive desperatus, ve
violentus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chainan, lamentatio, vel possessio
eorum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Malaleel, laudans deum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jared, descendens, sive roborans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Enoch, dedicatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mathusale, mortis emissio; vel mortuus
