1Onomavtwn thðé 2Ebraièdi dialevktwé.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Euøa, zwhv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1173" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1173A"></COL> Sarae nomen non interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">sterilis</HI> , juxta 
fidem elementorum; sed pro voluntate Graecorum,
qui sententias Scripturae sacrae saepius usurpant pro
etymologiis; nam de Sara dictum est Gen. XI, 30;
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Erat autem Sarai sterilis</HI> . Non sum tamen nescius
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231173D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">basoreth</HI> , significare  <HI REND="ITALIC">siccitatem</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">sterilitatem</HI> ;
unde violenter Graeci suo more formatum intelligunt
forte nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sarai</HI> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>SavrjrJa, devsmh blepomevnh, hÞ steiðra,
hÞ aærcousa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1175"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Agar, auæth proshvlutoû, hÞ suntrevfousa,
hÞ proshluteuvousa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rebevkka, pollhú uJpomonhú, hÞ poikivlh,
hÞ pnohú aænwqen, hÞ carav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>DebovrjrJa, mevlissa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sepfovra, cavriû kaiú kavlloû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rachúl, provbaton, hÞ pnohú ijscurouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1175" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1175A"></COL> Apud Philonem  <HI REND="ITALIC">Lia</HI>  interpretatur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kopiwðsa,</FOREIGN>  et
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnaneuomevnh,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">laborans,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">renuens,</HI>  sive potius
 <HI REND="ITALIC">recusata,</HI>  ut nos Latine reddidimus: qua interpretationis
consonantia perspicue satis probatur, hujus
Fragmenti etymologias, si non omnes, saltem plures
a Philone mutuatas fuisse.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Leiva, kopiwðsa, hÞ ejmovcqhsen, hÞ ajnaneuomevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhrsabeeú, qugavthr dunatouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Saraaú,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1175" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1175A"></COL> Prius inter Graeca Fragmenta docet nos, hanc
vocem legi debere cum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>a, ajrcomevnh,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">subdita,</HI> 
sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae imperio alterius paret;</HI>  non autem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejrcomevnh,</FOREIGN> 
quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">venientem</HI>  sonat. Neque etymologiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">venientis</HI> 
patitur nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sarai,</HI>  si juxta proprietatem linguae
Hebraicae illud interpretemur. Nos vero cum errore
scriptum hic maluimus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejrcomevnh</FOREIGN>  quam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrcomevnh,</FOREIGN> 
propter morosos quosdam criticos qui codicum mss.
sphalmata venerantur.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejrcomevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qavmar, ajllaxavshû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1175" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1175A"></COL> Martian.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ aællaxen.</FOREIGN></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ hællaxen, hÞ
foivnix, hÞ pikrasmovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mariva, kurieuvousa, hæ pikraú qavlassa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mariaúm, fwtizwmevnh, hÞ fwtivzousa
aujtouúû, hÞ kuvrioû ejk gevnouû mou, hÞ
smuvrna qalassiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rouúq, pnohú, hÞ speuvdousa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1175" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1175A"></COL> Nominis Susannae recordatur Hieronymus in
Luca, non in veteri Testamento.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sousavnna, caraú aujtwðn, hÞ ajpostolikoún
krivnon, hÞ ajnavstasiû dovxhû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1175"><NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1175" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1175A"></COL> Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ARSENIKA.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ARSENIKWN.</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Fareúû, fragmovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1176" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1176A"></COL> Non satis liquet, quare  <HI REND="ITALIC">Esron</HI>  Graeci  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uålhn,</FOREIGN>  id
