Melius ac verius apud Hieronymum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Esron</HI> 
interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">sagittam vidit,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">atrium eorum:</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231176A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">es</HI> 
enim, sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">hhets</HI>  est  <HI REND="ITALIC">sagitta;</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231176A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">raa, vidit;</HI>  et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231176A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hhaser, atrium.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Esrwúm</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1175" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1175A"></COL> Mendose Martian. ex Regio ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Wsrwðm,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Osrom.</HI></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uålhn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aqaúm, uJyhlovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aminadaúb, eæqnoû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1176" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1176A"></COL> Vatic.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiqumhtikoún,</FOREIGN>  quod proprie  <HI REND="ITALIC">cupidum</HI>  sonat.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiqumhtovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1176" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1176A"></COL> Vitiose ex Regio scriptum erat  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nasswðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Nasson.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Naasswðn, ajnavpausiû aijwniva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salmwún, lavbe skeuðoû ejklektovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Booúz, eæleusiû dunathv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwbeúd, uJpotassovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iessaiú, ajnavyuxiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1176" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1176A"></COL> De David scriptum est Ps. CXVIII:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Incerta et occulta
sapientiae tuae manifestasti mihi;</HI>  ideo Graeci
nomini ejus affigunt hanc etymologiam,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cui parata
fuerunt abscondita.</HI>  Ad similes allegorias nusquam
attendit doctissimus Hieronymus: sed omnium vocabulorum
etymologias juxta proprietatem linguae
Hebraicae exprimere voluit, ut haec loco  <HI REND="ITALIC">David</HI>  interpretatur
 <HI REND="ITALIC">fortem manu,</HI>  a  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231176B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dai,</HI>  et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231176B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">jad; desiderabilem</HI> 
vero ex  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231176B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ava,</HI>  aut ex  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231176B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">amad,</HI>  id est,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desideravit,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">concupivit.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Dabiúd, pepoqhmevnoû, hÞ hjlehmevnoû, hÞ
iJkanoúû ceiriú, hÞ wßé hJtoivmastai taú
ajpovkrufa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1177"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Solomwðn, eijrhnikovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Roboaúm, ejn plhvqei laouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abiouúd, pathúr ejrcovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1177" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1177A"></COL> Insignis isthaec nominum corruptela irrepsit in
codices Latinos veteris Vulgatae Evangelii secundum
Matthaeum; nam in manuscripto perantiquo monasterii
hujus sancti Germani a Pratis sic scriptum reperi:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Roboam autem genuit Abiud; Abiud genuit
Asaph; Asaph genuit Josaphat.</HI>  Asa ergo corrupte
scribitur Asaph, quem florenti myrto comparant
Graeci propter virtutem ac pietatem singularem,
qua inter reges Judae celeberrimus memoratur.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Asaúf, muvrton× wåsper gaúr toú muvrton
qewreiðtai kaiú ceimwðnoû eujqaleúû,
kaiú eujwðdeû, ouåtw kaiú hJ iJstoriva twðn
dikaivwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwsafaút, kuvrioû krithvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwraúm, kuvrioû uåyouû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1177" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1177A"></COL> Plusquam violenter interpretatur apud Graecos
nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ozios, sororis illustres;</HI>  nec umquam Hebraeum
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231177A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Ozihau</HI>  significationem  <HI REND="ITALIC">sororis</HI>  habere
poterit, etsi vocabulum sursum deorsum accipiatur.
Lege itaque  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ochozias,</HI>  tum propter seriem generationum
IV Reg. VIII, 24, ubi non  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ozias,</HI>  sed  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ochosias</HI> 
filius est Joram, tum propter etymologiam
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajdelfhðû,</FOREIGN>  quae in  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231177B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Achasiahu,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ochosiau</HI>  utcumque
continetur:  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231177B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ahhoth,</HI>  enim, vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">achoth</HI> 
 <COL N="1178A"></COL> dicitur Latine  <HI REND="ITALIC">soror.</HI>  Deinde  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231178A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aze,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">achze</HI>  Chaldaice
dicitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">spectatus,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">conspicuus,</HI>  quod maxime
convenit cum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpifanhvû</FOREIGN>  Graecorum.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ozivaû, ajdelfhðû ejpifaneiðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwnavqan, kuvrioû aæmwmoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Acaz, krataivwma kurivou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sedekivaû, dikaiosuvnh kuvriou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1178" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1178A"></COL> De  <HI REND="ITALIC">Manasse</HI>  lactum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Madiam</HI>  vix mihi persuasissem,
