nullum genus corruptelarum ab exscriptoribus
librorum fuisse alienum. Hocque loco Lector meminisse
debet errore librariorum Graecorum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Enos</HI>  supra
scriptum esse pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Noe;</HI>  unde mirum non est, si
pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Manasse Madiam;</HI>  et pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Josia, Jesba</HI>  legamus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Madiaúm, kavqou wßde.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Iesbaú, throumevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Samavreia, ajnapauomevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Raasswðn, fwðû qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Rwmelivou, kurivou ajnavpausiû eænqen.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Farawú, movscoû keratisthvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baqouhúl, parqevnoû ijscurav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cetouvra, mikrav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1177" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1177A"></COL> Haud bene Martian. ex Reg.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Et</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Et.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ceút, skeuðoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ghrswún, pavroikoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1177" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1177A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Ex</HI>  solemni  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>b</FOREIGN>  in  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>m</FOREIGN>  vitiosa mutatione in mss. legerat
