deduci non inficiar.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>yavllousa fwnhú, oujk ejn ojrgavnwé.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iarevr, ejpivbleyiû kurivou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Canaaún, proskunwðn ajnomivan.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1179" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1179A"></COL> A Graeculo scriptore inferioris aevi adjectae videntur
hujusmodi interpretationes nominum Gomer,
et trium consequentium. Cujus scriptoris imperitiam
castigat Hieronymus libro Quaest. Hebr. in
Genesim, dicens:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sunt autem Gomer, Galutae: Magog.
Scythae: Madai, Medi: Javan, Jones, qui et
Graeci: Thubal, Iberi, qui et Hispani . . . Mosoch, Cappadoces:
unde et urbs hodie apud eos Mazaca dicitur . . . .
Thiras, Thraces, quorum non satis immutatum
 <COL N="1180A"></COL> est vocabulum.</HI>  etc.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gomeúr,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1179" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1179A"></COL> Legesis  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qraðkeû.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Thraces;</HI>  gentis nomen.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qwvrakeû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Magwúg, paðn eæqnoû, hÞ</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1179" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1179A"></COL> Nihil dubium, ita rescribendum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Magwúg,</FOREIGN>  pro corrupto
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nagwún,</FOREIGN>  quod Regius ms. praefert, Vatican.
quoque: sicuti et hoc  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðsai fulaiú</FOREIGN>  pro uno verbo
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pamfiliú,</FOREIGN>  vel ut minus male Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pamfiliva.</FOREIGN>  Manifestum
librarii vitium hic loci tum sensus prodit, tum
 <COL N="1179B"></COL> praecipue Origenianum Lexicon mox adnectendum.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Magwúg, thðxiû, hÞ paðn eæqnoû, hÞ paðsai fulaiv,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Magog, liquefactio,
 <COL N="1180A"></COL> vel omnis natio, vel omnes tribus.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðsai fulaiv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mavdai,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1180" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1180A"></COL> Vitiose Martian.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavrtoi.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">parti.</HI>  Emendat Vatic.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pavrqoi.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mosoúl, toxeuthvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qhvraû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1180" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1180A"></COL> Hanc praefero archetypi Vatic. lectionem, pro
