formatum sit a verbo  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231180B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nazar,</HI>  vel a voce  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231180B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nezir,</HI> 
quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">florem</HI>  aliquando fignificare docent Eruditi.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nebrwúd,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1180" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1180A"></COL> In Vatic. est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnqerwðn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnqhrwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Babulwún, suvgcusiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Oreúk makravn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sennaaúr, eiødoû qhriwvdhû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Assouúr, mesopotamiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nineuhð, deomevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="j" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1180" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1180B"></COL> Idem Vatic.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Canouaún.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Canaaún deú ejgevnnhse tovn Sidwðna.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sidwún, eæxelqe ejn krivsei.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ceqaqaú, aJmartavnwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1181"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aijlaúm, oijkoumevnhn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Arfaxaúd, oJrwvmenoû ejk pantovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Araúm, uJyhlovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwúb, ajgaphtoúû kurivou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gameúr, lhnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mosoúc, toxeuthvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Eber, diaperwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iektaún, mikrofuhvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elmwdaúd, kinouvmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1181" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1181A"></COL> Insignes hic sunt vocabulorum depravationes
apud LXX et in Regio codice ms. Nihil enim esse
potuit depravatius, quam scribere  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aithiai,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jaree;
Atharoudam,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aduram,</HI>  et praecipue  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ethecmal,</HI> 
pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Decla</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ebal.</HI>  Consulat studiosus Lector
caput X Geneseos, 26, usque ad 30, pervidebit statim
articulum Hebraeum accusativi casus  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231181A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">eth</HI>  copulatum
esse imperitia Graecorum cum suo nomine.
Verbi gratia  <HI REND="ITALIC">Atharoudam</HI>  nomen est  <HI REND="ITALIC">Adouram</HI>  cum
articulo praecedenti  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231181B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">eth.</HI>  vel,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ath,</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231181B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">athadouram.</HI>  Ubi insuper observare debemus Graecos
legere  <HI REND="ITALIC">Daleth</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Resch,</HI>  et vicissim  <HI REND="ITALIC">Resch</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Daleth.</HI> 
Idem erit judicium de praecedenti,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aithiai,</HI>  quod
ex  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231181C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ath,</HI>  et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231181C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">jare</HI>  factum est, mutato  <HI REND="ITALIC">r</HI>  cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">i</HI>  ultimo
in voce  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aithiai,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Athiare.</HI>  Caetera duo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ethecmal</HI> 
et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ethemmimael,</HI>  eamdem habent depravationis
causam et originem.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aijqivai, katabaivnonteû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aqaroudaúm, oåraton uJyhlovn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1181" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1181A"></COL> Minus corrupte Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ozaúl,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Ozal,</HI>  et mox  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Eqekbaúl</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ethecbal.</HI>  Persequi autem haec piget verborum monstra.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ozaún, ejlafrouúû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Eqekmaúl, nefelwvdhû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Eqemmimahúl, pathvr mou ijscurovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Wfeúd, fwðû qerapeivaû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eujeilaút deiðxon wßde.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Araúm, ejscavth.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1182" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1182A"></COL> Hieronymus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jobab</HI>  Latine expressit  <HI REND="ITALIC">mago patre;</HI> 
quia  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ob</HI>  Hebraice est  <HI REND="ITALIC">magus,</HI>  et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ab, pater.</HI> 
Graeci etymologiam deducunt ex  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">jaab, desideravit.</HI> 
vel  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ahab, dilexit.</HI>  Primam autem syllabam
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Jo</HI>  nominis  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Jao,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jehova,</HI>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Domini</HI> 
compendiariam esse volunt.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwbaúb, ajgapwðn kuvrion.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nacwúr, devhsiû ejscavth.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Awút, lelutrwmevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1182" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1182A"></COL> Ut perspicuum sit cuique legenti, cur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Chaldaei
dicantur magi</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">harioli,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">quasi daemonia,</HI>  operae
pretium putavi isthaec observasse cum Eruditis: Hieronymus
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Chasdim, quasi daemonia</HI>  interpretatus
est, accipiendo scilicet  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cha</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">sicut,</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sed</HI> 
pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">daemonia,</HI>  et mutando  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sin</HI>  cum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">lamed,</HI>  ut sit
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231182B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Chaldim</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Chasdim.</HI>  Rursus quia Chaldaei
astrologiam judiciariam invenerunt, omnes  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mathematici,
genethliaci, magi, harioli,</HI>  et alii eamdem artem
profitentes,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Chaldaei</HI>  appellati sunt: hinc apud
Graecos  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mavnteiû</FOREIGN>  ac  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mavgoi</FOREIGN>  interpretantur.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Caldaiðoi, mavnteiû, mavgoi.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Suceúm, wømoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqhvl, oiøkoû ijscurovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aggaiú, eJorthv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Amarfaú, sumboliva ponhrav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ariwúl, levwn, hÞ oænoma basilevwû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1181" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1181A"></COL> Vitiosius in Regio erat  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Escevod</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Escheod.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Escwúd, bovtruû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1181" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1181A"></COL> Ita paulo rectius ex Vatic. reposuimus. Martian.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Anaaún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Anaan</HI>  legerat, apposueratque in Hieronymiano
 <COL N="1182A"></COL> syllabo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ana, responsio,</HI>  etc.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Wnaaún, ajnomiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cwbaúl, ajrkeið.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Damaskoúû, ajnavbasiû siwphrav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bavtoû, miðsoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cananaivwn,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1182" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1182A"></COL> Erat ex Reg.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proskunovntwn ajnomivan.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proskunouvntwn ajnomivaé.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1AmorjrJaivwn, mikrwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ferezaivwn,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1182" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1182A"></COL> Legerat uno verbo Martian, ex Regio,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skoliwðnoû,</FOREIGN> 
verteratque  <HI REND="ITALIC">tortuosum reddentis.</HI>  Vide hoc idem nomen
supra in altero Fragmento.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skoliwðn wJû ejpiú oæfewn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1183"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gergesaivwn, katoivkhsiû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183"></COL> Vatic.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mataivou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vani.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mataiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iebousaivwn, kataiscunomevnwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Darwðn, kibwtovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183"></COL> Sina allegorice dicitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">visio sempiterna</HI>  propter
res gestas ibidem, crebraque Mosis alloquia cum
Deo. Noli igitur id accipere tamquam nominis etymologiam,
sed ut mysticam, aut typicam interpretationem
 <COL N="1184"></COL> montis Sinai, in quo Deus apparuit, legem
Hebraeis statuens. Idipsum sentiamus de nomine
Israelis consequenti, cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">populus fortis</HI>  interpretatur.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sinaú,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183"></COL> In Origeniano autem Lexico inferius excudendo
 <COL N="1184"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aærsiû</FOREIGN>  legitur, sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">elevatio,</HI>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oårasiû</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">visio.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oårasiû aijwniva, hÞ mivsoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Israhúl, oJrwðn qeoún, hÞ laoúû ijscurovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM></LIST></DIV2> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="1183"><HEAD COM="1183"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hieronymus.</HI> 
LIBER NOMINUM
HEBRAICORUM.</HEAD> <COL N="1174"></COL> <LIST COM="1174"><ITEM>Eva, vita, aut vae, aut calamitas.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sara, princeps.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1176"></COL> Agar, advena, vel conversa.</ITEM> <ITEM>Rebecca, multa patientia, vel multum
accepit, sive patientia.</ITEM> <ITEM>Debora, apis, vel loquax.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sephora, avis ejus, vel pulchritudo
ejus, sive placens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Rachel, ovis, vel videns principium,
aut visio sceleris, etc.</ITEM> <ITEM>Lia, laboriosa.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bethsabee, filia juramenti.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sarai, princeps mea.</ITEM> <ITEM>Thamar, palma, vel amara.</ITEM> <ITEM>Maria, sermone Syro domina nuncupatur.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mariam, plerique aestimant interpretari,
illuminant me isti,
vel illuminatrix, vel zmyrna
maris; sed mihi nequaquam
videtur. Melius autem est, ut
dicamus sonare eam stellam
maris, vel amarum mare.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ruth, festinans, aut videns, etc.</ITEM> <ITEM>Susanna, lilium, aut gratia ejus;
sed melius si femininum nomen
figuretur a lilio.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1176">VIRILIUM.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Phares, divisio, sive divisit.</ITEM> <ITEM>Esrom, sagittam vidit, sive atrium
eorum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aram, excelsus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aminadab, populus meus voluntarius.</ITEM> <ITEM>Naasson, quidam putant requietum
sonitum: sed melius est,
augurans, sive serpens eorum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Salmon, sensibilis, sive sensus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Booz, in quo robur, vel in ipso
fortitudo: sed melius in fortitudine.</ITEM> <ITEM>Obed, serviens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jessai, insulae libatio, sed melius
incensum.</ITEM> <ITEM>David, desiderabilis, aut fortis
manu.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1178"></COL> Salomon, pacificus, sive pacatus
erit.</ITEM> <ITEM>Roboam, impetus populi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abia, pater dominus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Asa, tollens, vel attollens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Josaphat, ipse judicans; sed melius,
dominus judicabit.</ITEM> <ITEM>Joram, ubi est excelsus? aut quis
est excelsus? sed melius, sublimabitur.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ozia, fortitudo domini.</ITEM> <ITEM>Joatham, consummatus, sive perfectus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Achaz, apprehende.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sedecias, justus dominus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Manasse, obliviosus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Josias, ubi est incensum domini?
vel salus Domini, etc.</ITEM> <ITEM>Samaria, custodita.</ITEM> <ITEM>Raason, cursus, vel complacitio,
sive placentia, quam significantius
Graeci  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujdokivan</FOREIGN>  vocant.</ITEM> <ITEM>Romelias, excelsus domini.</ITEM> <ITEM>Pharao, dissipator, sive discooperuit
eum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bathuel, virgo dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chettura, thymsama offerens, vel
copulata, aut juncta.</ITEM> <ITEM>Cheth, percutiens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Gersan, advena ibi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chaleb, quasi cor, aut omne cor,
vel canis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jefanne, innuit, vel innuens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elia, deus dominus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elisaeus, dei mei salus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chebron, conjugium, aut visio
sempiterna, etc.</ITEM> <ITEM>Asaph, congregans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Gelhoe, volutatio, sive decursus,
vel acervus pluens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Melcha, regina ejus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eden, voluptas, sive deliciae, vel
ornatus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Gedera, maceria, sive sepes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Maviael, qui est dominus, vel ex
vita deus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ada, testimonium.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sella, umbra ejus.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1180"></COL> Thobel, ductus ad luctum, vel conversus,
aut universa.</ITEM> <ITEM>Noema, decor, sive voluptas, vel
fides.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jared, descendens, sive roborans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chanaan,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>savloû</FOREIGN>  hoc est motus corum,
etc.</ITEM> <ITEM>Gomer, assumptio, sive consummatio,
etc.</ITEM> <ITEM>Magog, quod  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dwðma,</FOREIGN>  id est tectum,
vel de tecto.</ITEM> <ITEM>Madai, mensura, sive quam sufficienter.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mesech, prolongatio, vel certe
compressus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Thiras, timens, vel redimens, aut
superfluum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aschenez, ignis sic aspersus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elisa, deus meus, vel ejus salus,
vel ad insulam, vel dei mei salvatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Tharsis, exploratores laetitiae, vel
gaudii.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chetim, confracti.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chus, Aethiops.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mesraim, hostes eorum, vel Aegyptus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aegyptus, tribulatio coangustans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Phut, Libya, sive oris declinatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Seba, captus, sive captivitas, vel
certe convertens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Dedan, judicans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chus, Aethiops.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nemrod, tyrannus, vel profugus,
aut transgressor.</ITEM> <ITEM>Babylon, confusio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Orech, longitudo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sennaar, excussio dentium, sive
fetor eorum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Assur, dirigens, vel beatus, aut
gradiens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nineve, pulchra, vel germen pulchritudinis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chanaan, motus eorum, vel negotiator,
aut humilis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sidona, venatio moeroris.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chethaeus, mentis excessus, sive
fixus, vel abscissus.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1182"></COL> Elam, saeculi, vel orbis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Arphaxad, sanans depopulationem.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aram, excelsus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Job, magus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Gomer, assumptio sive consummatio,
vel perfectio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mesech, prolongatio, sive defectio,
aut certe compressus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eber, transitorem.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jectan, parvulus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elmodad, ad matrem ejus praecipuam,
sive dei mensura.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jaree, luna.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aduram, generatio excelsa.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aizel, pergens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Decla, subtile, sive palmata, Ebal,
vallis vetus, sive acervus lapidum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abimael, pater meus a Deo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ophir, irritum, vel in herbosum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aevila, dolens, sive parturiens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aran, iracunde, vel decor.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jobab, mago patre, sive distillans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nachor, requies luminis, vel obsecratio
novissima.</ITEM> <ITEM>Lot, vinctus, sive declinatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chaldaei, quasi daemonia, vel quasi
ubera, sive feroces.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sychem, humeri.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bethel, domus dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aggai, quaestio, vel festivitas.</ITEM> <ITEM>Amaraphal, dixit ut caderet.</ITEM> <ITEM>Arioch, ebrius, vel ebrietas.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eschol, botrus, sive ignis omnis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Onam, dolor, vel tristitia eorum,
etc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et</HI>  On, iniquitas.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chobal, condemnatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Damascus, sanguinis potus, sive
sanguinis osculum, vel sanguis
sacci.</ITEM> <ITEM>Batus, nomen mensurae.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chananaei, negotiatores, sive hic
pauperculus, aut praeparati, vel
humilitas.</ITEM> <ITEM>Amorrhaei, amari, vel loquentes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Pherezaei, separati, sive absque
muro, vel separantes, sive disseminati,
vel fructificantes.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1184"></COL> Gergesaei, colonum ejicientes, sive
advenae propinquantes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jebusaei, calcati, sive praesepe.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aaron, mons fortitudinis, sive
mons fortis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sinai, amphora mea, sive mensura
mea, vel mandatum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Israel, est videre Deum, sive vir,
aut mens videns Deum; sed melius,
rectus Dei.</ITEM></LIST></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="1184"><HEAD COM="1184"><HI REND="ITALIC">FRAGMENTUM QUINTUM.</HI> <NOTE TYPE=chad ANCHORED=N COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183"></COL> In Migne, the sections of text, headed  <HI REND="ITALIC">Interpretatio Latina, Codex Vaticanus</HI>  and  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hieronymus</HI>  are printed in parallel.</NOTE></HEAD> <COL N="1183"></COL> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="1183"><HEAD COM="1183"><HI REND="ITALIC">Interpretatio Latina.</HI> 
DICTIONES
SECUNDUM ELEMENTA
LINGUAE HEBRAICAE.</HEAD> <COL N="1183"></COL> <LIST COM="1183"><CAPTION COM="1183">A</CAPTION> <ITEM>Asara, ingratus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Adonai, domine.</ITEM> <ITEM>Adon, propheta, dupliciter dicitur.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abenezer, lapis adjuvans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ano, gloria.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abael, a Deo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ada et Seila, terra et spes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abigaea, patris sublimis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ammanitae, curvatura.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abba, pater.</ITEM> <ITEM>Azael, ablegatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Adamatha, terra rufa.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ariel, leo validi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aaron, ecce opus, ecce.</ITEM> <ITEM>Adonibezec, domini adjutorium.</ITEM> <ITEM>Abiel, laus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aenos, homo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Aria, leo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ammon, et Moab, de genere meo,
et de patre meo.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1185"></COL> Alleluia, laudate, hymnis celebrate
dominum.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185">B</CAPTION> <ITEM>Bethel, domus dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bethleem, domus panis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bethania, domus gloriae.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bethphage, domus prosperi successus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bersabee, filia potentis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bathuel, qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">est</HI>  venientis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bosor, caro.</ITEM> <ITEM>Beliar, quaesitor.</ITEM> <ITEM>Beelzeebul, daemon Baceloseorum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bamam, mater.</ITEM> <ITEM>Baalim, daemonia.</ITEM> <ITEM>Berecthra, musca vocatur.</ITEM> <ITEM>Bal, daemon.</ITEM> <ITEM>Barjona, fili columbae, vel fili
Jona.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185">G</CAPTION> <ITEM>Gamaliel, loquax dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Gedeon, trahens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Galaad, ab uno.</ITEM> <ITEM>Gaza, advena.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185">D.</CAPTION> <ITEM>Degoen, natio non natio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Drus Mambri, qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">est</HI>  filii.</ITEM> <ITEM>Dalida, judicium mihi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Udrosos Aermon, ros glorificatus.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185"><COL N="1187"></COL> E</CAPTION> <ITEM>Eloai, deus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eloethe, deus venit.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ephraim, consolator.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eliezer, dei auxilium; qui etiam
transfertur David.</ITEM> <ITEM>Exarmathem, de emissione.</ITEM> <ITEM>Exanathom, a me veniens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ephrata, consolationis.</ITEM> <ITEM>In terram Moab, in genus patris
mei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eirosodalamites, per spiritum introeuntem.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ex monte Ephraim, de monte consolationis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elcana, potens gloria.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elisaeus, virtus dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>In virgulio Sabec, in plantatione
forti, sive aureo olere.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ex Agge, de requie.</ITEM> <ITEM>In terra Naim, in terra laudantium.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elimelec, dei regia.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ex Arira, de resistente spiritu.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eber, Hebraei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Evinas interpretatur, qui ostendit
serpentes, cujus numerus est
666.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eliacim, dei sepositus.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1187">Z</CAPTION> <ITEM>Zacchaeus, victor.</ITEM> <ITEM>Zorobabel, qui fuit Salathiel, de
confusione.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1187"><COL N="1190"></COL> H</CAPTION> <ITEM>Heliu, fortis Domini.</ITEM> <ITEM>Esau, resurgens: vocatus est Aedom,
deficiens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Venit in Elim, venit in locum dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Venit in Aphecca, venit in tenebroso.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1190">TH</CAPTION> <ITEM>Filia Bathuel, filia venientis fortis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Thala, convallis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Tharsis, quae urendi vim habet.</ITEM> <ITEM>Thara, ignis spiritus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Thabor, prodi ab spiritu.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1190">I</CAPTION> <ITEM>Jesus, salvator.</ITEM> <ITEM>Josias, salvatus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jao, invisibilis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jochabel, super arcam.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jou, vide a Domino.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jephthae, accipiens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jesus Josedech, salvator pacis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jordanes, confirmatus, vel terra
ultima, deficiens, vel bruchus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Idumaea, deficiens, aut bruchus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jerusalem, ipsius  <HI REND="ITALIC">est</HI>  spiritus gratiae.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jesus Nave, salvator justitiae.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ismael, exauditio fortis, vel respice
deus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jaser, domini auxilium.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jonathan, columbus veniens, aut
venit.</ITEM> <ITEM>Japheth, latitudo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jonadam, columba unius.</ITEM> <ITEM>Joannes, baptizator.</ITEM> <ITEM>Josedec, justitia.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jechonias, mundus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Joacim, sepositus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Isesias, obumbrans.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1190">K</CAPTION> <ITEM>Kedar, <NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1190" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1190A"></COL> Hebraice  <HI REND="ITALIC">testa</HI>  dicitur  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231190A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hheres,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">cheres;</HI> 
tenebrae autem  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231190A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Cedar.</HI>  Videant itaque Graeci
quam violenter  <HI REND="ITALIC">Kedar</HI>  ab ipsis sit interpretatum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">testacea.</HI></NOTE>  testacca.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1191"></COL> Karbasinum, impollutum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Kades, caelebs.</ITEM> <ITEM>Kadon, sanctus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Et erat homo de Armathem Siphae,
et erat homo de emissione
splendoris.</ITEM> <ITEM>Et nomen illi Elcana, et nomen
illi fortis gloria.</ITEM> <ITEM>Koilas, mare.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1191">L</CAPTION> <ITEM>Lamech, qui  <HI REND="ITALIC">est</HI>  in praeceptis.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1191">M</CAPTION> <ITEM>Melloth, regina parva.</ITEM> <ITEM>Moyses, aquae ablatio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Moysi, non aqua est.</ITEM> <ITEM>Merra, amaritudo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Maria, domina nostra.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mabri, filii.</ITEM> <ITEM>Melchisedec, rex pacis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Maselech, mutus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Maozin, quemcumque tandem.</ITEM> <ITEM>Moabitae, locusta.</ITEM> <ITEM>Moab. de patre meo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Manaan illi, oblationem illi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Manasse, a resistente.</ITEM> <ITEM>Manoe, aliquando.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mestraim, niger Aegyptius.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mamona, divitiae.</ITEM> <ITEM>Melcho, reges.</ITEM> <ITEM>Man, quid?</ITEM> <ITEM>Melche, rex.</ITEM> <ITEM>Mazer, de longe, vocatus est vero
dominus.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1193"></COL> Beatus es Simon, beatus obaudiens.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1193">N</CAPTION> <ITEM>Nazar, flos.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nazaraeus, floribus variegatus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Naeinam, prae somno capite nutans.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nomin, dulcis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nachor, mei ipsius.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nabal, corvus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nephthaleim, opitulatio, et Nephthalim,
convertit me.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nachael, ego deus veniens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Nabuthe, a spiritu veniens.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1193">O</CAPTION> <ITEM>Hollam, ingrediens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Holiba, egrediens.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1193">P</CAPTION> <ITEM>Phasec, redemptio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Pathura, mensa.</ITEM> <ITEM>Apponebantur in Be, diabolo dicto.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1193">R</CAPTION> <ITEM>Raca, vacuus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Raph, flatus patris.</ITEM> <ITEM>Rachel, flatus potentis.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1193">S</CAPTION> <ITEM>Sabaoth, virtutum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sampson, sol.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sipha, splendor.</ITEM> <ITEM>Siphan, resistens faciebus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Solomon, gratiarum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Samarites, auditus loquentis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Somanites, qui audivit.</ITEM> <ITEM>Samuel, petitio a deo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Selom, locus ubi tabernaculum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sion, sitiens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sina, sitis.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1195"></COL> Silom, venustus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Seila, spes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Siloam, emissus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sepphora, gratia huic spirationi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Salem, gratia.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sith, resurrectio.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sem, resurrexi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Somam, obediens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sabaim, Aethiopes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Satanas, affligens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Samuel, minister audiens deum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sicima, ascendens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Saul, expetitus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Seraphim, spiritus resurrectionis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sume, congelatio aquae.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sigor, quae resurgit, vel humilitas.</ITEM> <ITEM>Saphecca, in tenebroso.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sennaar, putredo.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sabbata, sanctificationes.</ITEM> <ITEM>Seraphim, stabant, spiritus resurgentes,
lumini stabant.</ITEM> <ITEM>Salathiel, gratia venientis Daniel.</ITEM> <ITEM>Saba, regina Aethiopiae, hanc vocant
ethnici Sibyllam.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1195">V</CAPTION> <ITEM>Filium Barachiae, filium benedicti.</ITEM> <ITEM>Filii Noemin, Malon et Cheleon,
quia ingredere, abi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Filii Eliu, filii fortis domini.</ITEM> <ITEM>Filius Thebel, filius mensurae.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1195">PH</CAPTION> <ITEM>Phennana, luminis gloria Phanuel,
apparens.</ITEM> <ITEM>Vox ex Rama, vox de sublimi.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1195">CH</CAPTION> <ITEM>Cherubim, alae.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1197"></COL> Cherubim, ala.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chelcias, fundamentum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chettim, insulis luctarum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Chelaeon, proficiscens.</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1197">PS</CAPTION> <ITEM>Psalmus super Idithum, Psalmus super
uno judice.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anathom, mei venientis.</ITEM> <ITEM>De terra Benjamin, de terra filii
doloris.</ITEM> <ITEM>De Babylone, de confusione.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jessias, qui Sophoniae, inumbrans,
ejus qui stare facit terram.</ITEM> <ITEM>Ephud, manifestatio, et veritas.</ITEM> <ITEM>Pharia, filia Pharaonis. Venit ut
lavaretur, et invenit Moysem
adhuc infantem. Et cum suspexisset
in coelum, ait: O
unus Deus infinita habens nomina!
Hinc ethnici vocant eam Eisitan,
666.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nomen est</HI>  hominis
habentis hunc numerum in Apocalypsi
Joannis. Hoc est, venturus
est ex Medis ad debellandos fideles.
De quo et Isaias dicit: Ecce
suscitabo super vos Medos, et
reliqua.</ITEM> <ITEM>Baruch, benedictus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Eloai, deus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Adonai, dominus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Jao, invisibilis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Sabaoth, virtutum.</ITEM> <ITEM>Elimaz, sermo dei.</ITEM> <ITEM>Marsippion, assensus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Opelos, ingluvies ventris.</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Thðé</FOREIGN>  plintho, scortationi.</ITEM> <ITEM>Cherubim, scientia multiplicata, vel
alae.</ITEM> <ITEM>Amen, confirmatio vere sic esse.</ITEM></LIST></DIV2> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="1197"><HEAD COM="1197"><HI REND="ITALIC">Codex Vaticanus.</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>LEXEIS KATA STOICEION
THS EBRAIDOS DIALEKTOU.</FOREIGN></HEAD> <COL N="1183"></COL> <LIST COM="1183"><CAPTION COM="1183">A</CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Asaraú, ajcavristoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Adonai0, kuvrie.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183A"></COL> Graecorum annotationem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>disswðû prolevgetai</FOREIGN>  explicat
sufficienter etymologia nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Adon</HI>  apud
Hieronymum, qui idem vocabulum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Addo</HI>  Latine
reddidit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">servus ejus</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">testis ejus. Adon</HI>  igitur dupliciter
scribitur, nempe cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">b, Abdo,</HI>  et cum duplici
 <HI REND="ITALIC">d. Addo,</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231183A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Abdo</HI>  autem exprimitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">servus ejus;</HI>  et
 <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231183A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Addo testis ejus.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Adwn, profhvthû, disswðû prolevgetai.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abenezeúr, livqoû bohqwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183A"></COL> In Vatic, est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Anaú,</FOREIGN>  Ana.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Anwð, dovxa.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183A"></COL> Vide in primo Fragmento quod de  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abel</HI>  etymologia
jam observatum est.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abahúl, ajpoú qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Adaú kaiú Seeilaú, ghð kaiú ejlpivû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abigaiða, patroúû uJyivstou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ammaniðtai, kamphv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abbaú, pathvr.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Azahúl,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183A"></COL> Corrupte lectum a Martian.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxasulhú</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxapostolhú,</FOREIGN> 
ut ex Vatic. emendamus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxapostolhv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Adamaqaú, ghð purjrJav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Arihúl, levwn ijscurovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Aarwún, ijdouú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1184" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1184A"></COL> Vatic. compendiosa scriptura  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>praiçdouú,</FOREIGN>  quod aliter
legi possit. Mox quoque  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Adonibezevk.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>praðgma, ijdouv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1183" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1183A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Adonibezec</HI>  confundunt Graeci cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Adonezer,</HI>  qui
 <COL N="1184A"></COL> in  <HI REND="ITALIC">Domini adjutorium</HI>  vertitur.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Adonibezhúk, kurivou bohvqeia.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abihúl, aiønoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aijnwðû, aænqrwpoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ariva, levwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1184" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1184A"></COL> De hisce nominibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ammon</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Moab</HI>  Hieronymum
audiamus pulchre disserentem:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Moab,</HI>  inquit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">interpretatur ex patre, et totum nomen etymologiam
habet. Ammon vero, cujus quasi causa nominis redditur,
filius generis mei, sive, ut melius est in Hebraeo,
filius populi mei, sic derivatur, ut ex parte sensus nominis,
et ex parte ipse sit sermo.</HI>  AMMI ( <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231184A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">enim, a
quo dicti sunt Ammonitae, vocatur populus meus.</HI>  Sic
libro Quaest. Hebr. in Genesim.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ammwún kaiú Mwaúb, ejk touð gevnouû mou,
kaiú ejk touð patrovû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1185"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Allhlouvia, aijnevsate, uJmnhvsate toún
kuvrion</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>B</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beqhúl, oiøkoû qeouð</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqleeúm, oiøkoû aærtou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqaniva, oiøkoû dovxhû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqfaghð, oiøkoû ejpitucivaû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhrsabeeú, qugavthr dunatouð</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baqouhúl, oJ touð ejrcomevnou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bosoúr, savrx</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Belivar</FOREIGN> , <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1185" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1185B"></COL> Perperam ex Regio Martian.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkzhthvû</FOREIGN>  legerat pro
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkzhththúû</FOREIGN> , quod ex Vatic. restituimus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkzhththvû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beelzeebouúl</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1185" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1185A"></COL> Auctoritate Scripturae certi sumus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Beelzebub</HI> 
Deum fuisse Accaronitarum: Achas enim ex lapsu
decumbens, I Samuelis I, 4, mittit viros, qui de
valetudine ipsius consulant  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231185A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Baal-zebub,
deum Accaron;</HI>  ubi LXX Interpretes habent  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baaúl
muivaû</FOREIGN> , id est  <HI REND="ITALIC">Baal muscae.</HI>  Sic ergo vocatum est
idolum, quod incolae urbis Accaron in Palaestina
colebant; illudque daemonium in muscas perniciosas
habere imperium et has ex sua regione abigere
credebant. Scio etiam apud Ethnicos Jovem fuisse
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>muaiðon</FOREIGN>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpomuaiðon</FOREIGN> , id est Jovem  <HI REND="ITALIC">muscarium,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">muscaram
depulsorem,</HI>  qui  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajcwúr</FOREIGN>  appellatus sit. Unde Plin.
lib. X:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Invocant Cyreniaci Achorem deum, muscarum
multitudine pestilentiam afferente, quae protinus intererunt,
quando litatum est illi Deo.</HI>  Cyreniaca, regio
Africae, regnum complectitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Barcae,</HI>  quod verbum
 <COL N="1185B"></COL> accedit aliquo modo ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">Baceloseon</HI>  codicis manuscripti
Graeci, quo docemur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Beelzebub</HI>  daemonium
fuisse  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bakhlwsevwn</FOREIGN> . Sed forte scribere debuit amanuensis
 <COL N="1186A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bakhvlwn</FOREIGN> , quod significaret Beelzebub deum
esse scortatorum; nam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bavkhloû</FOREIGN>  apud Graecos est
vir magnae staturae, sed stultus et mulierosus, eviratus
etiam et spado. Quae profecto quadrani optime ad
effeminatos Matri deorum, sive Priapo consecratos,
de quibus abunde disserit Hieronymus lib. I Comment.
in Osee cap. IV. Confer ista cum iis quae leguntur
infra in Lexico Origeniano ad vocem  <HI REND="ITALIC">Beelzebul.</HI></NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>daivmwn</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1185" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1185B"></COL> Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bakhlwvsewû</FOREIGN> . Ut vero dissimulem Martianaeum
in hujus explicatione vocis infeliciter hariolari,
facile assentiar Clerico conjicienti ex Origeniano
Lexico, ubi hoc idem  <HI REND="ITALIC">Beelzebul</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>daivmwn kaphleuúû</FOREIGN>  interpretatur,
reponendum hic  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaphleuvsewn</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bakhlwvsewn</FOREIGN> ,
quod factum videtur litterarum fere similium
inter se mutatione, K scilicet in B, et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eu</FOREIGN>  in  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>w</FOREIGN> , Tunc
autem vertas in Latino,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Daemon cauponarius,</HI>  sive
 <HI REND="ITALIC">cauponarii quaestus.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bakhlwsevwn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1185" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1185B"></COL> Sic emendamus ope Vaticani ms. ad Hebraicae
linguae proprietatem, quae  <HI REND="ITALIC">matrem</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231185B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">am,</HI>  vocat, cujus
 <COL N="1186B"></COL> est radix  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231186A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">amam,</HI>  quae in Arabico resonat.
Martianaeus vero satis vitiose  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Balaúm</FOREIGN> , et Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Balam</HI> 
supposuit, quin etiam in Hieronymiano laterculo  <HI REND="ITALIC">Balaam,
vamus,</HI>  etc.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bamavm, hJ mhthvr</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baaliúm, daimovnia</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Berecqraú, muiða kaleiðtai</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baúl, daivmwn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bariwnað, uiJeú peristeraúû, hÞ</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1186" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1186B"></COL> Alteram  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uiJeú</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fili,</HI>  vocem, quae penes Martianaeum
deerat, supplemus ex Vaticano.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uiJeú
1Iwnað</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>G</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gamalihúl, oJ lalhtoúû qeouð</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gedewún, eålkwn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Galaaúd, ajpoú eJnovû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gavza, pavroikoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>D</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Degwhún, eæqnoû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1186" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1186B"></COL> Pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujk</FOREIGN>  in Vatic. est distinctus verbis  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouj hj</FOREIGN> . Haud
vero opinor  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dagon</HI>  idolum hic denotari.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujk eæqnoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1186" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1186A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Druðû mabreið</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Drus mabre,</HI>  est  <HI REND="ITALIC">quercus Mamre</HI> 
in Genesi.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mabre</HI>  autem Graeci et infra in Lexico
Origeniano, interpretantur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ touð uiJouð</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui est filii,</HI> 
sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">de filio,</HI>  quia illud nomen legunt cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">b</HI>  in medio,
ut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ma</HI>  sit praepositio  <HI REND="ITALIC">a,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex; bre</HI>  vero, aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">bar, filius</HI> 
intelligatur.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Druðû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1186" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1186B"></COL> Martian.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mabreið</FOREIGN> , ut ex ejus annotatione vides.
Vitiose ex Regio descripserat, vertitque  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mabre.</HI>  Nos
ex Vatic. emendamus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mambriú</FOREIGN> : quemadmodum et alia
quaedam leviora inferius.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mambriú, oJ touð uiJouð</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Dalidaú, krivsiû ejmoiv</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1186" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1186A"></COL> Graecorum imperitia confundit verba pure Graeca
cum nominibus Hebraicis, ut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Oudrosos,</HI>  quod
Graecum est prorsus, non Hebraeum. Deinde praepositiones
Graecas copulat cum vocibus Hebraeis,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxarmaqeún,
ejxanaqwúm</FOREIGN>  id est, de  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ramathaim, de Anathoth.</HI> 
 <COL N="1186B"></COL> Has omnes ineptias redarguunt nomina pure scripta
in columna Hieronymiana.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Oujdrovsoû 1Aermwðn, drovsoû ejndoxazomevnh</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1185"><COL N="1187"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>E</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elwai0, oJ qeovû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1187" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1187A"></COL> Vocabula  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eloe,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eloethe</HI>  non recenset Hieronymus
in libro Nominum Hebraicorum; sed in Epistola
quam scripsit ad Marcellam de decem nominibus
Dei, dicit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Etoim</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eloe</HI>  significare  <HI REND="ITALIC">Deum; Maranatha</HI> 
autem interpretatur supra in nominibus de Epist.
I ad Corinthios,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dominus noster venit;</HI>  additque
Syrum esse vocabulum. Ex quo manifestum est  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231187A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">atha,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">ethe</HI>  exprimi  <HI REND="ITALIC">venit;</HI>  et Graecorum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elweqeú</FOREIGN> 
merito interpretari,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Deus venit.</HI></NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elweqeú, qeoúû hølqen</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Efrai0m, paravklhtoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elievzer, qeouð bohvqeia, oÝû kaiú metermhneuvetai
Dabiúd</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Exarmaqeúm, ejk probolhðû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Exanaqwúm, ejx ejmouð ejrcovmenoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Efraqaú, paraklhvsewû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1187" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1187A"></COL> Ludunt hoc modo Graeci in recensendis nominibus
Hebraicis ac eorum etymologiis; phrases enim
et sententias recitant integras, ut unicum nomen
Hebraicum exponant. Haec tamquam superflua abjecit
Hieronymus, Hebraicorum vocabulorum interpretationi
totus intentus in libro Nominum.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eijû ghðn Mwaúb, eijû gevnoû patrovû mou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1187" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1187A"></COL> Voluit forte exscriptor Graecus ponere  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iJerosolumivthû</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Hierosolymites;</HI>  quae vox magis sonat Graece
partim et Hebraice,  <HI REND="ITALIC">per spiritum introeuntem,</HI>  quam
 <COL N="1188A"></COL> nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Odollamites.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eijrosodalamivthû, diaú pneuvmatoû touð
eijsercomevnou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ex oærouû 1Efrai0m, ejx oærouû paraklhvsewû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elkanaú, ijscuvousa</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1187" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1187B"></COL> Idem legerat  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dovxhû</FOREIGN>  et sexto casu verterat  <HI REND="ITALIC">gloria.</HI> 
Paulo inferius hoc idem nomen occurrit sub K littera.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaiú oænoma aujtwðé 1Elkanaú</FOREIGN> , quod rursum interpretatur
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijscuroúû dovxa</FOREIGN>  in Vatic., non  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dovxhû</FOREIGN> , ut ex Regio Martian.
descripsit. Ex Origeniano autem Lexico, ubi
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qeouð kthðsiû hÞ dovxa</FOREIGN>  dicitur, legendum hic colligit
Clericus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijscuvontoû dovsiû</FOREIGN>  aut  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dwðra</FOREIGN> , ut vox deducatur
ab  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231187B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">el,</HI>  quod est  <HI REND="ITALIC">potens,</HI>  et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231187B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hhanan, gratificatus
est, dedit.</HI>  Nobis Vaticani archetypi fide nihil est
antiquius.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dovxa</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elissaiðoû, duvnamiû qeouð</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1En futwðé Sabeúk</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1188" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1188A"></COL> De hoc nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sabech</HI>  fuse disputat Hieronymus
libro Quaest. Hebr. in Genesim, cap. 22.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn futwðé dunatwðé</FOREIGN> , <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1187" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1187B"></COL> Voces  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hægoun crusolacavnwé</FOREIGN>  hic Vaticanus non
agnoscit. Apponit autem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>crusolacavnwé</FOREIGN>  tantum ad
libri oram.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hægoun crusolacavnwé</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ex Aggeú ejx ajnapauvsewû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1En ghðé Nai0m, ejn ghðé uJmnouvntwn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elimeleúk, qeouð basivleion</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ex Ariraú, ejx ajnqistamevnou pneuvmatoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>4Eber, 2Ebraiðoi</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1188" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1188A"></COL> Bestiae numerus hic est in Apocalypsi Joannis
XIII, 18. At non legimus in Scriptura sacra nomen
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Evinas,</HI>  quod ita confictum esse videtur a Graecis,
quia numerice valet 666. Nam E, valet 5;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>u</FOREIGN> , 400;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>i</FOREIGN> ,
10;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>n</FOREIGN>  50;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>a</FOREIGN>  1,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>s</FOREIGN> , 200; quae simul juncta efficiunt
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>c x û</FOREIGN> , id est, 666. Inter arcana Hebraeorum mysteria,
modus iste computandi appellatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Guematria,</HI> 
estque aequivalentia sensus ex aequivalentia
numerica dictionum, quam Graeci tabulam Pythagoricam
nuncupare dicuntur. Non mihi licet ignorare
circa numerum bestiae multa fuisse a diversis ultro
citroque excogitata: sed cum sint pleraque manifeste
falsa ac reproba; alia autem dubia ac incerta,
his omnibus recensendis conjecturis jam supersedeo.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>EuJiçnaðû, eJrmhneuvetai</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1187" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1187B"></COL> Deduci hanc etymologiam puto e duabus Hebraeis
vocibus, nempe verbo  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231187C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">indicavit, ostendit,</HI> 
et nomine  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231187C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">serpens.</HI>  Nec tamen ignoro  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231187C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Hovia,</HI>  Chaldaicum nomen,  <HI REND="ITALIC">serpentem</HI>  significare;
 <COL N="1188B"></COL> unde Clem. Alex. in Protrept. ad Gent. p. 9:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kataú</FOREIGN> , inquit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thún ajkribhð twðn eJbraivwn fwnhún toú oænoma toú EuJia
dasunovmenon eJrmhneuvetai oÞfiû hJ qhvleia</FOREIGN> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si accurate vox
Hebraica spectetur, nomen Hevia aspiratum exponitur
serpens femina.</HI>  Ipsum vero nomen  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Euçinaðû</FOREIGN>  unum
fuerit e multis, quae olim excogitata sunt ad divinandum
illud Antichristi, cujus elementa numerice
sumpta, 666, summam confectura dicuntur in Apocalypsi.
Ex his quae Irenaeus, lib. V, cap. 30, affert,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eujanqaû</FOREIGN>  huic propius accedit in litteris: istud vero
ingenio jus multo est, et commoda prae caeteris interpretatione
gaudet. Vide laudatum Irenaei locum,
in eumque Fevardentii notas. Hic porro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oæfiû</FOREIGN> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">serpens,</HI> 
in recto singulari, restituendum videtur pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oæfiû</FOREIGN> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">serpentes.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ deivxaû ojfeiðû.
ouß oJ ajrisqmoúû cxû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Eliakivm, qeouð ajpokeivmenoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1187"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Z</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Zakcaiðoû, nikhthvû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1188" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1188B"></COL> Corrupte legerat Martian.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Zorombakeúl</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Zorombacel.</HI> 
