ijscurouð</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qalaú, koilavû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qarseiðû</FOREIGN> , <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1189B"></COL> In Vatic. uno verbo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJbaitikhú</FOREIGN> , pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJ kaustikhv</FOREIGN> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJ kaustikhv</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qaraú, fwtoúû pneuvmatoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Qaboúr, deuðro ajpoú pneuvmatoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1189"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>I</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ihsouðû, swthvr</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwsivaû, swzovmenoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1189A"></COL> Confer ista cum Prologomenis nostris in divinam
Bibliothecam sancti Hieronymi, ubi de nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jao</HI> 
disputavimus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iavw, ajovratoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1189A"></COL> Graecorum etymologia manifestat, ubi fuerit Domini
gloria, non significantiam nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jochabed,</HI> 
quod S. Hieronymus interpretatur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi est Domini
gloria.</HI>  Verum est ergo Domini gloriam super arcam
habitasse; scriptum enim legimus II Samuelis. VI, 2:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut adducerent arcam Dei, super quam invocatum est
nomen Domini exercituum, sedentis in Cherubim super
eam:</HI>  sed, ut jam dixi, in vera historia falsam reperimus
nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jochabed</HI>  etymologiam.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwcabeúl, uJpeúr kibwtouð</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iouð, iæde ejx aujqevntou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iefqaeú, lambavnwn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1189A"></COL> Constans est error Graecorum in etymologia verbi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sedec,</HI>  quod hic quoque confuse accipiunt pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">salem;</HI> 
 <COL N="1190A"></COL> ut supra in nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Melchisedec,</HI>  quem  <HI REND="ITALIC">regem pacis</HI> 
interpretantur. Jesum Nave etiam post pauca confundunt
cum Jesu Josedec, quod ex serie praesenti
nominum probari potest, in qua Graeci tandem  <HI REND="ITALIC">Josedec</HI> 
interpretantur  <HI REND="ITALIC">justitiam.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ihsouðû oJ touð 1Iwsedeúk, swthúr oJ thðû
eijrhvnhû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iordavnhû, katabebhkwúû, hÞ ghð ejscavth,
ejkleivpousa, hÞ brouðcoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Idoumaiva, ejkleivpousa, hÞ brouðcoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ierousalhvm, aujtouð pneuðma cavritoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ihsruðû oJ touð Nauhð, swthúr oJ thðû dikaiosuvnhû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ismahúl, ajkohú ijscurouð, hÞ ejpivde oJ
qeovû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iashúr, aujqevntou bohvqeia</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwnavqan, peristeroúû ejrcovmenoû, hÞ eærcetai</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iavfeq, platusmovû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1189A"></COL> Malim ex Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwnadavb</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jonadab,</HI>  quod Hieronymus
interpretatur.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Domini spontaneus.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwnadaúm, peristeraú eJnoúû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwavnnhû</FOREIGN> , <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1190" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1190A"></COL> Ineptam interpretationem nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joannis</HI>  caveat
Lector;  <HI REND="ITALIC">baptistes</HI>  namque cognomen est Joannis propter
officium baptizandi a Deo ipsi commissum, non
etymologia nominis sui, quam apud Hieron. requirere
cuique licet.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>baptisthvû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwsedeúk, dikaiosuvnh</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ieconivaû, kaqavrioû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwakeiúm, ajpokeivmenoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Isesivaû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1189" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1189A"></COL> Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iessivaû</FOREIGN> . Quae praeferenda sit lectio, alii
judicent. Profecto  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jezeciae</HI>  nomen ita depravari, vix
credam. Immo vero  <HI REND="ITALIC">Josiam</HI>  innui arbitror; sic enim
 <COL N="1190A"></COL> infra, ad litteram  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Y</FOREIGN> , alter  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iessivaû oJ touð Sofonivou</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jessias
Sophoniae filius,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>suskiavzwn</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">obumbrans</HI>  vertitur.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>suskiavzwn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1189"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>K</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Khdaúr</FOREIGN> , <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1190" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1190A"></COL> Haud ita existimo, vocem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ojstrakivnh</FOREIGN> , hic  <HI REND="ITALIC">testaceam</HI> 
significare, sed  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ostracinem,</HI>  nomine proprio. Innuere
voluit Graecus libelli hujus auctor, regionem  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cedar</HI> 
eamdem esse, quae  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ostracine</HI>  alio nomine dicitur.
 <COL N="1191B"></COL> Nimirum saepe in hisce Fragmentis nomina Hebraea
non ex ejus linguae proprietate, sed per alia nomina,
quae deinde obtinuerunt, aut per symbola interpretantur.
Exemplo sit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Shlwúm. tovpoû oåpou hJ skhnhv.</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Silo, locus ubi Tabernaculum fuit,</HI>  etc.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ojstrakivnh</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1191"></COL> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1191" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1191A"></COL> In libro Estheris cap. I, 6, legimus nomen  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231191A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Karpas,</HI>  significatque  <HI REND="ITALIC">colorem carbasiaum:</HI>  sed observavi
nullum Hebraeum vocabulum ex volumine
Estheris, vel ex Paralipomenis recenseri ab Hieronymo
in libro Nominum. Unde igitur derivatum sit
in praesentem collectionem, si non inde fluxit, vix
possum conjicere.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Karbasinoún, ajmivanton.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1191" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1191A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Kades</HI>  supra col. 545 interpretatur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJgiasmovû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sanctificatio,</HI> 
et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Kadon,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJgivaû,</FOREIGN>  hoc est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sanctae.</HI>  Quae diversae
interpretationes proclivi lapsu librariorum
Graecorum exortae videntur, dum scribunt  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aægamoû</FOREIGN> 
pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJgiasmovû,</FOREIGN>  et caetera similiter.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kavdhû, aægamoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kadwðn, aågioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1191" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1191A"></COL> Initium hoc est prioris voluminis Samuelis, cujus
versiculum primum fere integrum otiose describunt,
ut duo vocabula tantummodo interpretentur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Armathaim</HI>  scilicet, et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Elcana.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaiú høn aænqrwpoû, ejx 1Armaqeúm</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1191" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1191B"></COL> Martian. ex Regio  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>simfahv.</FOREIGN>  LXX in Vatic. cod.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sifaú,</FOREIGN>  legunt: al.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Swfivm.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sifahú,
kaiú høn aænqrwpoû ejk probolhðû</FOREIGN> 
 <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1191" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1191B"></COL> Vocem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fwtismouð,</FOREIGN>  Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">splendoris,</HI>  quam Martian.
