analogia est.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>potev.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mestraiúm, mevlaû aijguvptioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mamwnað, plouðtoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Melcwð, basileiðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1192" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1192B"></COL> Hunc titulum quem Martian. Regium exemplar
secutus omittit, ex Vatic suffecimus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Maún, tiv_</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Melchú basileuvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1192" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1192A"></COL> Locus omnino depravatus in Graeco; pro corruptis
enim  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mazhúr ejpimhðkoû ejklhvqh deú kuvrioû,</FOREIGN>  id est,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Mazer, de longe, vocatus est vero dominus,</HI>  scribendum
videtur juxta fidem contextus sacri, Deut. XXIII,
2:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mamzer (non ingredietur)</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû ejkklhsivan Kurivou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in
Ecclesiam Domini.</HI>  Alioqum absurdissimus erit in
Graeco sensus, nec auctoritate Scripturae umquam
poterit comprobari.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mazhúr,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="i" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1192" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1192B"></COL> Vatic. uno verbo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpivmiktoû,</FOREIGN>  quod est  <HI REND="ITALIC">mixtus.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiú mhðkoû, ejklhvqh deú kuvrioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1193"></COL> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1193" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1193A"></COL> Ex Evangelio secundum Matthaeum cap. XVI, 17,
sumpta sunt isthaec; sed corrupte pro more exscriptorum,
qui legere debuerant  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Makavrioû eij Sivmwn,</FOREIGN>  non
autem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijsimwn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Makavrioû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1193" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1193A"></COL> Sic emendat Vatic. In Regio autem, quod ex
Martian. annotatione intelligis, erat uno verbo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijsimwn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eiø Sivmwn, makavrioû oJ
uJpakouvwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>N</FOREIGN> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Navzar, aænqoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nazhraiðoû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1193" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1193A"></COL> Recurrebat error, quem in superiore secundo
Fragmento castigavimus, scilicet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxisqimevnoû.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">obstupefactus,</HI> 
pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxhnqismevnoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">floribus variegatus,</HI>  quemadmodum
 <COL N="1193B"></COL> ex Vatic. reponimus. Vide quae ibi observamus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxhnqismevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Naeinaúm, nustavzwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nomiún, glukeiða.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nacwúr, ejmouð aujtouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Navbal, kovrax.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1193" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1193B"></COL> Isthaec  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú Nefqaliúm sunanevstreyevn me,</FOREIGN>  in Vatic.
ms. non habentur, et superius quoque in secundo
Fragmento desiderari annotavimus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nefqaleiúm, ajntivlhyiû, kaiú Nefqaliúm,
sunanevstreyevn me.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nacahúl, ejgwú qeoúû ejrcovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nabouqeú, ajpoú pneuvmatoû ejrcovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>O</FOREIGN> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ollaúm, eijsercomevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Olivba, ejxercomevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1193"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>P</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Paseúk, luvtrwsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Paqouraú, travpeza.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1193" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1193A"></COL> Unde hauserint Graeci hanc sententiam, nondum
agnovi; sed nullum est dubium de nomine  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhð,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">be,</HI>  quo daemonium indicare volunt, sive illud sit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bel,</HI> 
sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">Belial</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Baal,</HI>  quorum frequens est memoria
in libris sacris. Apud Hesychium hujus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhð</FOREIGN>  manifesta
sunt indicia:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhðloû,</FOREIGN>  inquit,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujranoúû, kaiú Zeuúû
Poseidwðnoû uiJoúû,</FOREIGN>  hoc est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Belus, coelum, aut deus Neptuni
filius;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhðloû</FOREIGN>  autem per contractionem dici
potuit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhð,</FOREIGN>  ut sonaret idola et daemonia ethnicorum.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Parevqento ejn twðé</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1193" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1193B"></COL> Haec male a Graeculo amanuensi habita, et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bhúl,</FOREIGN> 
pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bhð</FOREIGN>  reponendum, facile omnes intelligunt; sic
tamen praefert et Vatic. Videtur, inquit Clericus, ab
eo ex quo haec desumpta sunt, mentio facta de eo,
