in Graeco  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aijnevsewû,</FOREIGN>  id est  <HI REND="ITALIC">laudis;</HI>  Hieronymus
enim abjiciens hanc etymologiam, utpote violentam,
manifeste declarat Graecis fuisse propriam, et
sibi alienam. Legebat igitur ipse in Graecorum
 <COL N="1208B"></COL> exemplaribus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aijnevsewû,</FOREIGN>  non  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnevsewû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnevsewû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Apollwúû, sunavgwn aujtouvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Apfivou fovrw, ejleuqerivaû karpoforivaû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Aradoû, katabivbasiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1209"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Araraút, marturiva, hÞ</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1209" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1209A"></COL> Pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tepilumevnh</FOREIGN>  codicis manuscripti, legendum,
