in Regio ms. atque adeo in Martianaei quoque
editione. Sed et vox  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>suvmptwma</FOREIGN> , quae nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aseneth</HI> 
etymologia est, deerat: unde quae ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">Asur</HI>  pertinent
verba  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>euæqumoû hÞ Mesopotamiva,</FOREIGN>  misere distorta sunt
junctaque eidem  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aseneth,</HI>  quasi propria ejus expositio,
cui nihil minus respondet. Nos ex Vatic. archetypo
 <COL N="1212A"></COL> lacunam supplevimus, et veram cuique voci,
interpretationem in Latino quoque syllabo restituimus.</NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ashrwúq, makarismoiv</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Asouúr, euæqumoû, hÞ Mesopotamiva</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1211" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1211A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Assarion</HI>  Graecum verbum est, Matth. X, 29, a
Latina voce  <HI REND="ITALIC">as, assis.</HI>  Obolus est Italicus. Juxta Graecam
etymologiam pars est decima nummi, aut denarius
 <COL N="1212A"></COL> noster aereus. Nihil tamen affirmo in re mihi
satis incerta, et dubia.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Assavrion, dekavnoumon</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Astavrth, 1Afrodivth, hÞ kaiú 1Astarwvq</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Auægoustoû, eJortavzwn, hÞ ktivsiû, eJorthú
prostiqemevnh</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aujsivthû, gevnoû boulhðû, hÞ bouleuomevnhû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Acaaúb, ajdelfoúû patrovû mou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Acaièa, ajdelfovthû aujtwðn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Acivezer, ajdelfovû mou</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1212" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1212A"></COL> Emendamus ad fidem Vatic.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bohvqeia</FOREIGN>  pro quo
Martian. ex Regio  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bohqiú</FOREIGN> , tametsi, Corrupte, inquit,
 <COL N="1212B"></COL> scriptum videtur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bohqiú</FOREIGN> , pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bohvqei</FOREIGN>  aut  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bohvqeia</FOREIGN> .
