 <HI REND="ITALIC">commorationem,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">villam:</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kovluboû,
eæpauliû</FOREIGN> . Non igitur scriptoris Graeci vestigiis inhaereamus,
ut cum ipso legamus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kovluboû</FOREIGN> , et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kolubistaiú</FOREIGN> ;
sed cum Hesychio  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kovlluboû</FOREIGN>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kollubistaiú</FOREIGN> . Est autem
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kovlluboû</FOREIGN>  juxta eumdem Hesychium,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eiædoû nomivsmatoû,
kaiú oJ ejn twðé calkwðé kecaragmevnoû bouðû</FOREIGN> ,
hoc est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">species
numismatis, et in quo</HI>  numulo  <HI REND="ITALIC">aereo impressa erat imago
bovis.</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kollubistaiú</FOREIGN>  porro, de quibus frequens mentio
 <COL N="1232B"></COL> in sacrosancto Evangelio,  <HI REND="ITALIC">trapezytae</HI>  fuerunt et  <HI REND="ITALIC">numularii,</HI> 
qui argenteos aureosve nummos permutabant
minutis, quales oboli sunt, etc.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú
Kolubistaiv</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1233"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Korbaún, prosforaú, dwðron.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Korivnqoû, politeiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1233" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1233A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Cosymbi,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">nodis</HI>  accipiuntur Exodi XXVIII, ubi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">nodi tunicarum ex bysso, et tunica nodis substricta.</HI> 
Huic sensui conveniunt verba consequentia in codice
Graeco, nodos enim significant arcte vestes astringentes.
De  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cosymbo</HI>  autem haec habet Hesychius:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kossuvmbh, kaiú kovssumboû, ejgkovmbwma kaiú perivzwma aijguvption,
kaiú ejgkombouðtai.</FOREIGN>  Docet ergo Hesychius  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cosymbon</HI> 
indumentum esse Aegyptium, et ornamentum
quasi innodatum et colligatum. Alii volunt  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgkovmbwma</FOREIGN> 
fuisse genus vestimenti in nodum constricti, quo
servi utebantur. At huic opinioni repugnant ea quae
a Graecis subjuncta sunt; nimirum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cosymbos</HI>  etiam
dictos  <HI REND="ITALIC">inaurata</HI>  quaedam ornamenta, sicut  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhnivskoû</FOREIGN> 
qui ornamentum dicitur collare, sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">monile</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">torques.</HI> 
Caetera verba, quia omnino corrupta depravataque
leguntur in codice manuscripto Graeco, non
interpretamur. Putavit unus e nostris linguae Graecae
peritus legi posse  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aællon aæssouû eæcwn, ajmfivkurta</FOREIGN> :
ut sit sensus, aliam esse interpretationem qua  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kovsumboû</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">vestis</HI>  dicatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">habens oculos,</HI>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ocellata,</HI> 
 <COL N="1234A"></COL> vel etiam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kovsumboi</FOREIGN>  erunt ligna ad onera portanda,
hoc est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajmfivkurta</FOREIGN> : Non omittimus tunicam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kosumbwtoún</FOREIGN> 
Exodi XXVIII, 4, esse tunicam  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum cirris,</HI>  qui bene
dispositi ornamento sunt vestibus. Consule August.
Quaest. 114 in Exod.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kovsumboi, ajnavlaboi, hÞ ajnakombwtikoiú,
sfiktoiú, hÞ kecruswmevna, wJû
mhnivskoû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1233" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1233A"></COL> Videtur, inquit Clericus, legendum,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû mhnivskoû,
ejpij wæmoiû sunevcwn ajmfivkurta,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut lunula, quae in humeris
continet ligna utrinque incurva,</HI>  quibus onera
nonnulla feruntur. Qua de re vide Suidam Aemilii
Porti.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejllovnoû souúû eæcwn ajmfivkurta.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Krivsoû, gnwðsiû dunathv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kuvproû, skuqrwpiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kurinaiðoû, klhronovmoû ajnhvr.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kwðla, fwnhú aujtwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Krivth, klhvsewû, hÞ ktivsewn, teleiwvsewû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1233" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1233A"></COL> Martian. ex vitiosa in Regio codice litterarum
metathesi, legerat  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kavluyin</FOREIGN> : annotavitque, Hebraice
quidem,  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231233A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Keli,</HI>  dici  <HI REND="ITALIC">vas,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">instrumentum:</HI>  sed
