in Daniel. cap. 3, de Naphtha disputavit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Salustius
scribit in Historiis,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod Naphtha sit genus fomitis
apud Persas, quo vel maxime nutriantur incendia.
Alii ossa olivarum quae projiciuntur cum amurca arefacta,
Naphthan appellari putant. Unde et Graece</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>purrivnh</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dicitur, ab eo quod</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>puðr,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">id est, ignem nutriat.</HI> 
Sic edoctus ab Hieronymo depravatam lectionem
manuscripti Graeci summa cum libertate castigavi,
 <COL N="1240A"></COL> scribens  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejlaiwðn</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxaiwðn</FOREIGN>  corrupto.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Navfqa, eiødovû ti Persikoún oå proú touð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1239"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>puroúû, wåû fasin, ejf1 eJautwðé eælkei
toú puðr, hÞ taú ajpotrughvmata, ojstað
twðn ejlaiwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nacwúr, ajnavpausiû fwtoúû, hÞ stevlecoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nessa, oJ 2Erwdivoû, pelargoúû legovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Necoqaú, ajrwmavtwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nhgaúr, ajnabaivnwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nikovlaoû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1239" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1239A"></COL> Falso excudit Martian. ex Regio  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujfrosuvnh,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">laetitia,</HI> 
