e compendiaria scriptura Graeca ms. codicis
mecum eliciunt eruditi sodales, quod interpretor
 <HI REND="ITALIC">fractos,</HI>  quia  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>rJwgalevoû</FOREIGN>  apud Homerum sonat  <HI REND="ITALIC">rimosum</HI> 
 <COL N="1244A"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">fractum.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>rJwgivlouû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1243"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>S</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabaiú, Aijqivopeû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1244" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1244A"></COL> Confundunt Graeci  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sahachar</HI>  cum nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bochor</HI> 
significante primogenitum.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabavcar, prwtovtokoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Savbbata, katavpausiû, hÞ ejpistromhú
aJgiavsmatoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1244" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1244A"></COL> Consule supra Quaestiones Hebraicas in Genesim,
ubi de  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sabec</HI>  disputavit Hierenymus. Graeci
allegorice illud nomen interpretantur propter liberationem
Isaac, cui Deus substituit hircum immolandum.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabeúk, aæfesiû, hæ iJlasmovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sadwúk, divkaioû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salaqihúl, aiæthsiû qeouð, hÞ touð ejrcomevnou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salmonaú, skiaú laouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salwún, eijrhneuvwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Samavreia, fulakhú aujtwðn pefaulismevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Samywún, hælioû aujtwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1245"></COL> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1245" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1245A"></COL> Corrupte  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sarabara,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Saraballa</HI>  scriptum docet
Hieronymus lib. I, Comment. in Dan. cap. III.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Saravbara, eiødoû uJpodhmavtwn Persikwðn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sarevqa, qlivyiû aærtou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1245" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1245A"></COL> Nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Satan</HI>  interpretantur Graeci  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trimovdion</FOREIGN> 
propter  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>savta triva</FOREIGN>  farinae, quorum meminit Christus
Matth. XIII, 33, et Luc XIII, 21, et Moses Gen.
XVIII, 6.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sataún, peirasmoúû ejpavrsewû, hÞ</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1245" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1245A"></COL> In Vatic. inter  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hæ</FOREIGN>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú</FOREIGN>  unius verbi spatium vacat.
Puta recipiendo nomini  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Savtoum</FOREIGN> , quod Latinum quidem
est, sed facile  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trimovdion</FOREIGN>  a Graecis potuit exponi,
ab exscriptore autem ob litterarum cum superiore
affinitatem omitti. Ad marg, quoque est nota  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Zt.</FOREIGN></NOTE> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú trimovdion</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Saouúl, aijthtoúû, hÞ kecrhmevnoû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sevbeai, euædromoû, hÞ plhvrhû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sedekivaû, dikaiosuvnh kurivou</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Seklaú, ejlpivû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1245" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1245A"></COL> Hoc nomen ex integro Vatic. restituit. Pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sekouðndoû</FOREIGN> ,
Martian. ex Regio legerat  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkouðndoû</FOREIGN> , ipsamque
vocem quasi alteram nominis Secla etymologiam illi
una serie subtexuit, vertitque  <HI REND="ITALIC">voluntarii.</HI>  In Notis
 <COL N="1245B"></COL> vero aestuat, nec tamen se extricat. Lego, inquit,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJkovntoû</FOREIGN> , ut sit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejlpiúû eJkovntoû</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">spes spontanei</HI>  seu  <HI REND="ITALIC">voluntarii,</HI> 
vel certe  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkousivwû ejpaivrwn</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ultro attollens.</HI> 
Nunc, ut vides, ipsaque Hieronymiana expositio a
nobis reposita persuadet, plana omnia sunt, atque
expedita.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sekouðndoû, ejpaivrwn</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Selmwðn, ajntapovdoma eijrhvnhû</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Seffariúm, bivbloi</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sepfovra, ejpivskeyiû wJraiva</FOREIGN> .</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Serouúc,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="c" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1245" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1245B"></COL> Est quidem in Vatic. hic atque infra  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpavrtima</FOREIGN> ,
quae vox utcumque  <HI REND="ITALIC">perfectionem</HI>  sonat; sed quod
Martianaeus ex Regio scribit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpavrthma</FOREIGN> , verius  <HI REND="ITALIC">profectio</HI> 
vertitur: unde et in Hieronymiano laterculo
 <HI REND="ITALIC">profectus</HI>  legendum conjecimus pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">perfectus.</HI>  Scilicet
ex  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpartavomai</FOREIGN>  verbo, quod est  <HI REND="ITALIC">longius digredior.</HI> 
 <COL N="1246A"></COL> Vide quae annotavimus col. 16.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpavrthma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Shúq, ajnavstasiû wJraiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1245" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1245A"></COL> Melius legeretur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Zaram</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Zeruch;</HI>  nam  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231245A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">zerua</HI>  significat  <HI REND="ITALIC">sativum,</HI>  et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231245A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">zara semen.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Serouúc</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1246" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1246A"></COL> Hunc quoque alium titulum Vatic. ms. ope restituimus,
et superiori propriam etymologiam vindicamus.
Martian. ex Regio,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpavrtima</FOREIGN>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Shwún</FOREIGN>  vocibus
detruncatis, quae hujus nominis expositio est,
priori junxerat una serie, manifesto autem mendo:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Serouúc, speirasmovû</FOREIGN> . Atque ita porro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>speirasmoúû</FOREIGN>  legerat
satis vitiose, verteratque  <HI REND="ITALIC">seminatio,</HI>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peirasmoúû</FOREIGN> ,
id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">tentatio,</HI>  quae verissima hujus est nominis etymologia.
 <COL N="1246B"></COL> Emendationem nostram ipsa Hieronymi
interpretatio, quam in ejus syllabo reposuimus, probat.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpavrtima.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Shwún, peirasmoúû qermovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sikavrioi, mequstaiv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sivkhma, ajnavpausiû, hæ oJmoivwsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabaú, rJavbdoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabawúq, twðn dunavmewn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1245" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1245A"></COL> Quia Oraculum erat in Sancto Sanctorum, hinc
ansam erroris sumunt Graeci ut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Caber,</HI>  sive potius
 <COL N="1246A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Daber</HI>  interpretentur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sanctum Sanctorum.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sabhúr, aågion aJgivwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1246" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1246B"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sahúl</FOREIGN> , pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iasahúl</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jasael,</HI>  usurpari opinor. Martian.
in Hieron. laterculo opposuerat,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sava, salvatoris.</HI> 
In Graeco autem pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qeouð</FOREIGN>  Vatic. habet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kurivou</FOREIGN> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sahúl, swthriva qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salhúm, eijrhvnh,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1246" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1246B"></COL> Martian.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpicarhúû</FOREIGN> , Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">laetabunda.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpivcariû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salmwðn, lavbe skeuðoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Salomwún, eijrhvnh, hæ cavriû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Samahúl, diavkonoû ajkouvwn qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1246" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1246A"></COL> Non etymologiam nominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Samuelis,</HI>  ut antea
