abs Hieronymo legendum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kakodaivmoneû</FOREIGN> , ipse enim
ita docet lib. V Comment. in Isai. cap. 13:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sirenae
autem</HI>  THANNIM  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocantur, quas nos aut daemones, aut
monstra quaedam, vel certe dracones magnos interpretati
sumus, qui cristati sunt et volantes.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkivdoneû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="h" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1246" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1246B"></COL> Quod suspicatur Martian. hic legendum,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kakodaivmoneû</FOREIGN> ,
nimis, inquit Clericus, abest a scriptura
Codicis, puta Regii, cui et Vatic. consentit. Porro
duplex putat ille hic mendum cubare: et primum
 <COL N="1247A"></COL> legendum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Seirhðneû</FOREIGN>  ex perpetuo usu linguae Graecae, et
ipsorum LXX Interpretum; deinde  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkidovneû</FOREIGN>  mutandum
in  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJlkuovnaû</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">halcyonas,</HI>  aut  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJlkhdovnaû</FOREIGN> , utrumque
enim videntur dixisse antiquiores Graeci, unde Latini
fecerunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">halcedones.</HI>  Sic interpretati sunt vocem
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>seirhún</FOREIGN>  Chrysostomus et Cyrillus Alexandrinus, ut
 <COL N="1247B"></COL> ostendit Samuel Bochartus Hierozoici part. II, lib. II,
cap. 14, qui item observat in Veterum scriptis,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJlkuovnaû</FOREIGN> , et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajhdovnaû</FOREIGN> , saepe a librariis mixta; quod
factum videtur propter affinitatem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJlkhdovnwn</FOREIGN> , et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajhdovnwn</FOREIGN> ,
ad sonum quod attinet, et quia  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJlkhdovneû</FOREIGN>  minus
erat usitatum.</NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1247"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sellaú, skiaú, hÞ skevph aujthv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Semeiè, ajkohv mou, eijsakousmovû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1247" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1247B"></COL> Corruptius ex Regio erat  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Seirnaceiriúm</FOREIGN> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sirnachirim.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sennaceiriúm, peirasmoúû, hÞ xhrasiva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Serafiúm, pneuðma ajnastavsewû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sigwúr, ajnistamevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Silwúm, ajpovlusiû auåth.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sibaú, strateiva, hÞ carav.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Sivkera, mevqusma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Silaúû, mesivthû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1247" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1247A"></COL> Locus obscurus, aptus maxime ad fovendas contrarias
