Aegyptii, et propter persecutionem, qua ipsi opprimebant
Hebraeos, etymologias hujusmodi confingunt
Graeci. Verbum autem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skotighð</FOREIGN>  formatum
volunt ex  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skotiva</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tenebrae,</HI>  et ex  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ghð,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">terra.</HI> 
Videsis col. 3, Annotationes nostras in nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aegyptus.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aiæguptoû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1255" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1255A"></COL> Emendandum, ut Clericus notat.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skotiva ghð.</FOREIGN> 
Tum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>diwvktria,</FOREIGN>  non  <HI REND="ITALIC">persecutionem,</HI>  ut Martian. vertit,
