legendum.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>diatrofhv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Azhka, sterevwsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1257" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1257A"></COL> Josue XVIII, 28,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eleph</HI>  nomen est urbis quod
Graeci corrupte legunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">Adepha;</HI>  et supra in libro Nominum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Aaleph.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Adelfaú, didaskaliva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ai0n, ojfqalmovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Azhvrh, ajnatolhv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aujqivtiû, boulhú.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Asida, eæleoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1257" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1257A"></COL> Hebraice  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231257A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Asaph,</HI>  cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Samech</HI>  in medio,
interpretatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">congregans:</HI>  si autem  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231257A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Asaph</HI>  habeat
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Sin,</HI>  Chaldaice  <HI REND="ITALIC">Astrologum</HI>  significat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Asouph</HI> 
igitur, quod Hieronymus  <HI REND="ITALIC">congregantem</HI>  transtulit,
Graeci  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>crhsmoún</FOREIGN>  reddiderunt. Est autem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>crhsmoúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">oraculum</HI> 
et  <HI REND="ITALIC">prophetia,</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">divinatio</HI>  apud Graecos; sive
id quod oraculo responsum est. Hinc  <HI REND="ITALIC">Asaph</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231257B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,
sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">Asouph</HI>  Chaldaeorum, videtur Graecorum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>crhsmovû.</FOREIGN> 
Asaph quoque prophetia celeberrimus.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Asouúf, crhsmovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Awúd, aiænesiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abelmaouðla, pevnqoû ajparcwðn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1257" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1257A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Ebion</HI>  intelligitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">pauper</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">egenus.</HI>  Confundunt
ergo Graeci nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Abiud</HI>  cum nomine  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231257C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ebion,</HI> 
 <COL N="1258"></COL> quod maxime vulgatum erat apud christianos.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abiouúd, peniva.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1258" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1258A"></COL> Corrupto  <HI REND="ITALIC">Asarom,</HI>  opposui  <HI REND="ITALIC">Esrom,</HI>  quia illud
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Asarom,</HI>  juxta sonum litterarum, potest significare
 <HI REND="ITALIC">altitudinem:</HI>  nam  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231258A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">rom,</HI>  exprimitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">altitudo.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Asarwúm, boulhðû uåyoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Aijavba, plhsmonhv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Araúf, eænedra.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Ari, fwðû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abihúl, pathvr mou qeovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Abievza, pathvr mou ijscuvû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Amalhúk, laoúû ejkklivnwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ammwún, laoúû ejqnwðn, hÞ povnou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Amhsaú, laoúû, eæparsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1258" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1258A"></COL> Nomina isthaec depravata docet adversa columna
