genus femininum pro masculino,  <HI REND="ITALIC">filiam</HI>  pro
 <HI REND="ITALIC">filium,</HI>  id est, Hebraice  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231258B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">bar,</HI>  pro  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231258B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">bath.</HI>  In altero
autem masculinum pro feminino, hoc est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qugavthr
eåbdomoû</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJbdovmh.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qugavthr ejklekthv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Basanithúû, aijscunovmenoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhrsabeeú, qugavthr eåbdomoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beelfegwúr, daivmwn Fegwvr.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Boswúr, savrx.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Barqolomaiðoû, uiJoúû eujloghmevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Boanergeúû, uiJoúû bronthðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqaniva, oiøkoû uJpakohðû,</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="9" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1258" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1258A"></COL> Abest hic particula  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vel,</HI>  ut ex superioribus
Graecis exemplaribus in promptu probatio est.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dovxhû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqfaghú, oiøkoû ejpitucivaû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhsaniva, oiøkoû bavtou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhliaúr, ejkzhvthsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baliún, daimovnion.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baúr ijwðna, uiJoúû peristeraðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Babulwún, suvgcusiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beniamiún, uiJoúû dexioúû, hÞ ojduvnhû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1259"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqeúl, oiøkoû qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baraú, ktivsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1259" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1259A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Bara</HI>  iterum legi debere monet nos etymologia
Graeca nominis hujus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Barsac.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Barsaúk, ejn ajsebeivaé.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bavlla, katapontismoúû, hÞ fuvrama.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bheivrei, frevata.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baqouhúl, qugavthr qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhqleevm, oiøkoû aærtou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>BhqevberjrJa, oiøkoû kataskeuhðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Biúq, oiøkoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="2" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1259" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1259A"></COL> Ex Matthaei Evangelio Hebraico sumptum videtur
hoc nomen ab Origene, quia ibi scriptum erat cap.
XXI, 9:  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231259A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">baruch abba,</HI>  cum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231259A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">He</HI>  emphatico
ut sit sensus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Benedictus ille qui venit,</HI>  etc.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Barouvcabe, eujloghmevnoû oJ pathvr.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Barouúc, eujloghmevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Bhelamwún, katachú oæclou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1259"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>G</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Geboueúl</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1259" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1259A"></COL> Non secundum etymologiam et fidem elementorum
dicitur Gelboe,  <HI REND="ITALIC">mons vanus factus;</HI>  sed propter
verba David,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Montes Gelboe, necros, nec pluvia veniant
super vos:</HI>  inde enim vani fiunt montes, et inanes ad
frugum semina fovenda. Similiter dicimus de monte
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Garizim,</HI>  qui juxta interpretationes allegoricas Graecorum
potest dici  <HI REND="ITALIC">mons redemptus,</HI>  eo quod benedictiones
positae leguntur super montem Garizim; maledictiones
 <COL N="1260A"></COL> vero super montem Hebal.</NOTE> ,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oæroû memataiwmevnon.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gavrixin, oæroû lelutrwmevnon.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gabrihúl, aænqrwpoû kaiú qeovû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>GovmorjrJa, stavsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ghwún, nhðloû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gaúd, ejpithvdeuma, hÞ tuvch.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gameúl, plhvrwsiû ajnwtevra.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1260" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1260A"></COL> Omisit particulam  <HI REND="ITALIC">En</HI>  in nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Engaddi,</HI>  quod
sonat  <HI REND="ITALIC">oculum tentationis:</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231260A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">en</HI>  namque  <HI REND="ITALIC">oculus</HI>  exprimitur,
et  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231260A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">gad, tentatio.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gaddiú, ojfqalmoúû</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1259" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1259A"></COL> Supra in I Fragmento ad hoc nomen Martianaeus
ipse  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peirathvrion,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">latronum receptaculum</HI>  interpretatus
est, pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">tentationem:</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpoú touð peiravzein,</FOREIGN>  quam etymologiam,
 <COL N="1260A"></COL> Clerico annotante, respuit significatio Hebraica
vocis  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231260B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Gad.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peirathrivou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gallaúd, mevtoikon marturivaû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Galilaiva, kulismoúû kurivou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gevrgesa, paroikiva ejkbeblhmevnoû</FOREIGN>  ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Pro</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkbeblhmevnh</FOREIGN> ).</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gabbaqaú, liqovstrwtoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Golgoqaú, kranivon.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gamihúl, lalhtoúû qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ghrsaúm, pavroikoû, xevnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1259"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>D</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Dauiúd, dunatoúû ceiriv.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Danihúl, krivsiû qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Daún, krivsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Damaskoúû, aiåmatoû fivlhma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1259"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>E</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elissaieú, qeouð duvnamiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elimeleúc, qeouð basivleion.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1260" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1260A"></COL> Corruptissime legimus in hoc exemplari Graeco
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Elilatous</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Evilat,</HI>  ut probat etymologia nominis,
et Lexicon Origenianum supra col. 627, in vocabulo
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Evelat.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elillatouúû, oijkoumevnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elkanaú, qeouð kthðma.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Edwúm, ejkleivpwn.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Efraúq, paravklhsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1260" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1260A"></COL> Interpretatur Graecus hoc nomen ac si scriptum
esset  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eldan,</HI>  nam  <HI REND="ITALIC">El</HI>  dicitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Deus,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dan</HI>  sonat judicium.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Edad</HI>  igitur posuit pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Elmodad,</HI>  aut pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Elmodan.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Edaúd, qeouð krivsiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Eleiú, qeouð.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eujfravthû, tapeinofrosuvnh.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Efrai0m, karpoforiva, hÞ paravklhtoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elisabeúq, qeouð aæfesiû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ezekivaû, kravtoû qeiðon.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="7" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1260" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1260A"></COL> Sicut corrupte  <HI REND="ITALIC">Emimyr</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">Emor,</HI>  ita pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oænoû</FOREIGN> 
potuit amanuensis scribere  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>povnoû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Emimuúr, povnoû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="1261"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Eliezeúr, oJ qeovû mou, bohqovû mou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Emmhún, mhtevreû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Engadiú, ojfqalmoúû ejrivfou.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1En</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1261" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1261A"></COL> Non  <HI REND="ITALIC">Enagallim,</HI>  sed  <HI REND="ITALIC">Engannim</HI>  forte legendum,
nisi obstet etymologia  <HI REND="ITALIC">Engannim,</HI>  qua interpretatur
