kaleiðtai</FOREIGN>  p. 413.</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Manasshðû, ejk lhvqhû,</FOREIGN>  p. 278.</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Melcaú, basivlissa,</FOREIGN>  p 430.</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1286" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1286A"></COL> Falsus est Philo, si putavit nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Melchisedec</HI> 
significare  <HI REND="ITALIC">regem pacis: sedec</HI>  enim  <HI REND="ITALIC">justum</HI>  sonat et
 <HI REND="ITALIC">justitiam,</HI>  non  <HI REND="ITALIC">pacem.</HI>  Rex igitur Salem, qualis erat
Melchisedec, idem est Latine, quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">rex pacis,</HI>  quia
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Salem</HI>  vertitur in  <HI REND="ITALIC">pacem.</HI>  Hujus etymologiae monitum
volumus lectorem, ne haereat in ambiguitate dictionum,
et interpretationis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Melchisedec.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Melcisedeúk, basileva te thðû eijrhvnhû,
