Hebraeo  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231287B" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Osee,</HI>  sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hosee.</HI>  De eo nomine haec
habet Hieronymus in cap. I Osee prophetae:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Osee
enim in lingua nostra salvatorem sonat: quod nomen
habuit etiam Josue filius Nun, antequam ei a Deo
vocabulum mutaretur. Non enim, ut male in Graecis
codicibus legitur et Latinis, Ause dictus est, quod
nihil omnino intelligitur, sed Osee, id est, salvator,
et additum est ejus nomini, Dominus, ut salvator
Domini diceretur.</HI>  Philo  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231287C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Osee</HI>  interpretatur
ac si legeretur Hebraice  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231287C" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">e ze.</HI></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>poioúû oußtoû,</FOREIGN>  p.
1063.</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Wr, fwðû.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <CAPTION COM="1287"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>P</FOREIGN></CAPTION> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Farawú, ajporjrJivptwn,</FOREIGN>  p. 172.</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Fuswún, eJrmhneuvetai stovmatoû ajlloièwsiû,</FOREIGN> p. 54.</ITEM> <ITEM><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Fouaú, ejruqroún eJrmhneuvetai,</FOREIGN>  p. 498.</ITEM> <ITEM><NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1287" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1287A"></COL> Nomen Hebraeum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0231287D" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Phithom</HI>  Graece ac Hebraice
